WEBVTT

1
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:50,717
[intriguing music]

2
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:04,689
[birds chirping]

3
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,032
This is good.

4
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:21,122
[man/narration] One day, out of nowhere,
I started seeing numbers.

5
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,109
[spoon clinking]

6
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:53,696
Ah.

7
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:57,283
{\an8}[doctor] What did you say?

8
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,202
{\an8}You can see ghosts?

9
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,370
{\an8}Pardon?

10
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:05,959
{\an8}You can see your past life?

11
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,627
Numbers...

12
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:10,421
[man/narration] The doctors said
they had no idea why.

13
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,392
- [rain pouring]
- [woman] Since it's raining, I made jeon.

14
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:24,561
It's good, right?

15
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:28,565
{\an8}[intriguing music continues]

16
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,069
Drink some water.

17
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:38,366
[man/narration] These numbers
only appeared when I ate...

18
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:39,909
No, no.

19
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:42,620
They only appeared
when I ate food my mom made.

20
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:46,749
And strangely,
those numbers went down one by one.

21
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:51,087
Ow!

22
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:53,089
That hurts!

23
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,591
Stop fooling around and eat.

24
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:57,594
I even made the anchovy broth
from scratch for you.

25
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:07,228
[man/narration] When did I start
seeing those numbers?

26
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,147
{\an8}- [Ha-jun's mother] Ha-jun!
- [TV news playing]

27
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,773
{\an8}Eat before you go, okay?

28
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:13,985
{\an8}[Ha-jun] I told you I'm late, Mom.
At this rate, I'll miss the exam.

29
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:16,154
{\an8}Wake him up quickly
and make him eat too, okay?

30
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:17,155
Hey, Jung Ha-min.

31
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:18,781
Your big brother is taking the CSAT.
You won't even show your face?

32
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:20,825
- That hurts my feelings.
- Here, here, here.

33
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,035
- Just one bite.
- Ah...

34
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:23,494
- [Ha-min's mother] Say "ah," hurry!
- Fine, fine.

35
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,497
I can't live because of you, Mom.

36
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:28,041
If I mess this up, it's all your fault.

37
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:30,501
Hyung, fighting.

38
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:31,794
Life is one big shot.

39
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:33,755
{\an8}One shot.

40
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:36,216
- I'm going.
- Just one more spoonful. Ah, ah.

41
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:38,426
- [customer] Thanks for the meal.
- [Ha-min's mother] Goodbye!

42
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:41,429
- [phone ringing]
- [tray clattering]

43
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:44,807
[calm music]

44
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:53,191
Aren't you supposed to be
taking your exam right now?

45
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:14,337
[Ha-min's mother/sobbing]
How can I bear losing my precious child?

46
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,649
[Ha-min's mother] Let's eat first.

47
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:36,526
You need to eat to come to your senses.

48
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:52,083
How can you eat, Mom?

49
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,547
Will a person die from skipping one meal?

50
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,217
If you hadn't told him to eat,

51
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:03,761
Hyung wouldn't have had to run in a hurry,

52
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,890
and he wouldn't have been hit by a car!

53
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:13,813
[Ha-min sobbing]

54
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:14,856
[Ha-min's mother] Fine.

55
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:17,150
It's all my fault.

56
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:19,736
It's all Mom's fault,

57
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:21,529
so eat first.

58
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:24,532
You haven't eaten for three whole days.

59
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:31,664
If you don't eat, Mom won't eat either.

60
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:34,083
Do you want to hold another funeral?

61
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:37,503
Damn it...

62
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,732
[mysterious music]

63
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,700
{\an8}What?

64
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:10,453
Mom.

65
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:13,122
You don't see that?

66
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,293
What?

67
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:23,966
Huh?

68
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,513
No, never mind.

69
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:31,808
[calm music]

70
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:43,194
[commotion]

71
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:45,279
[lively Christmas carol music]

72
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,829
[employee 1] All right, everyone,
gather over here.

73
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:55,581
It's hard to change people's taste
in soju, right?

74
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:56,749
But you know what?

75
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:58,751
My life is even harder.

76
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,461
- [employees laughing]
- Come on.

77
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:01,879
All right, today too,

78
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:04,507
let's change everyone in this industry
over to Hanryang!

79
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:05,967
[employees] Change them, change them!

80
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,760
Change them all over to Hanryang!

81
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,095
- [employee 1] All right, positions!
- [employees] Positions!

82
00:07:09,178 --> 00:07:10,513
- [employee 1] Okay, let's go.
- [employee 2] Okay.

83
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:12,598
[Ha-min] Ha...

84
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,852
- Boss.
- [employee 1] Oh, you're drinking Hanryang.

85
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:17,186
{\an8}[employee 2] Hanryang over Sanhae!

86
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,479
{\an8}[employee 3] Hanryang is in charge of great taste!

87
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:19,605
{\an8}[employee 2] Hanryang is art!

88
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,065
[employee 4] Here comes our Hanryang.

89
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:23,317
- [female employee] Oh, applause!
- [customers] Hanryang, Hanryang, Hanryang.

90
00:07:23,401 --> 00:07:24,819
Hanryang, Hanryang, Hanryang.

91
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:28,197
[customers cheering]

92
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:31,284
[employee 2] A thrill that shakes your heart.
This is Hanryang.

93
00:07:31,367 --> 00:07:35,246
[employee 4] If you drink Hanryang soju today,
we'll give you hangover relief medicine as a gift.

94
00:07:35,329 --> 00:07:36,247
[customers cheering]

95
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:38,374
Oh my goodness.

96
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,466
[woman] Hello.

97
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:47,675
- [man 1] Yes.
- [woman] Hello.

98
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:48,843
Enjoy your meal.

99
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:50,011
[man 2] Today's menu is really good.

100
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:51,387
[woman] Thank you.

101
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:05,026
[light music playing]

102
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:12,533
It's good, but I just don't eat much.

103
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:13,826
I didn't say anything.

104
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:19,874
If you could eat only one thing
before you died, what would you eat?

105
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,835
- Anything...
- It can't be anything. You'll go to hell.

106
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:26,255
Raw fish bibimbap.

107
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:37,016
{\an8}[YouTuber/video] Two spoons.

108
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:39,185
{\an8}- Three spoons of soy sauce.
- [Ha-min] Three spoons of soy sauce.

109
00:08:39,268 --> 00:08:40,520
[YouTuber/video] There's no fixed amount
for soy sauce.

110
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:42,271
I just do it my own way.

111
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,607
Three big spoonfuls of sugar.

112
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:47,026
When you're mixing any kind of noodles,

113
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:49,237
{\an8}[bright music playing]

114
00:08:51,614 --> 00:08:53,449
{\an8}- always eat lots of garlic.
- [Ha-min] One spoon of garlic.

115
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,201
{\an8}[YouTuber/video]
This is sesame oil.

116
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,786
{\an8}- A friend sent it to me.
- What's next?

117
00:08:58,621 --> 00:08:59,580
{\an8}A whole lot of sesame oil.

118
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:01,374
- A whole lot of sesame oil?
- [woman 1/video] Huh! Sesame oil too?

119
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:02,416
[YouTuber/video] Add plenty of sesame oil...

120
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,043
[Ha-min] How much is "a whole lot"?

121
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:05,336
[woman 1/video]
How are you supposed to measure that?

122
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:08,005
[YouTuber/video]
Just measure it by how much you pour in.

123
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:09,465
It's more accurate than a spoon.

124
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:10,716
[door lock beeps]

125
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,176
[video continues playing]

126
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:14,512
- [Ha-min] You're home?
- [woman 2] Yeah.

127
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:15,721
- [door closes]
- [door lock beeps]

128
00:09:16,305 --> 00:09:17,139
What are you doing?

129
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:20,309
I felt bad that we couldn't
spend Christmas together.

130
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:22,228
- Oppa.
- [Ha-min] Yeah?

131
00:09:22,311 --> 00:09:24,730
You can't have everything.

132
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,899
Besides, we agreed to spend
New Year's together.

133
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:28,526
We're going to watch
the countdown together this year, right?

134
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:30,069
Of course.

135
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:31,362
You're hungry, right?

136
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:32,822
I'll make it quickly.

137
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:37,827
- But...
- [YouTuber/video] Mm!

138
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:41,581
Everyone else watches mukbangs
with young women.

139
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:42,957
Why do you only watch that grandma?

140
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:45,459
Does she reveal some secret technique?

141
00:09:46,168 --> 00:09:48,087
Because I miss my mom.

142
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:50,590
If you miss her, you can just go visit her.

143
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:54,218
Right, I could do that, but...

144
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,595
Anyway, my cooking skills
are legendary these days.

145
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,929
Is there anything else you want to eat?

146
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:58,681
Anything.

147
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,433
It can't be anything. You'll go to hell.

148
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:03,436
Seaweed soup.

149
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:06,397
Seaweed soup?
It's not even your birthday. Why seaweed soup?

150
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,773
Beef or clam?

151
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:08,816
Neither.

152
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:10,276
Then?

153
00:10:10,359 --> 00:10:12,320
When I lived at the orphanage,
there were a lot of kids,

154
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:14,280
so there was no beef
or clam in the seaweed soup.

155
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:16,115
They just boiled it
with some Dasida seasoning.

156
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:18,367
But strangely, I miss that taste.

157
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:19,744
Mm...

158
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:22,622
You deserve to be loved enough now.

159
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,624
I'll love you a whole lot.

160
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:29,086
Huh? For a passport?

161
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,382
[Ha-min] Huh? Oh, I forgot to tell you.

162
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:36,886
I'm planning to go on a trip
once I match schedules with my friends.

163
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,179
Keep one of these too.

164
00:10:38,262 --> 00:10:39,305
Why?

165
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:41,307
[Ha-min] Well,
you could use it as my funeral portrait.

166
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:43,392
What if I go on the trip
and never come back?

167
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:45,311
My mom doesn't have money.

168
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:47,146
Take money out of my account
and hold a funeral for me.

169
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:48,981
Shinhan, two, two, one, two.

170
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:50,483
NongHyup, three, three, zero, seven.

171
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:53,944
Why do you always go looking for worries?

172
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:54,987
Where do they sell them?

173
00:10:55,071 --> 00:10:58,574
Hey, our lives are on borrowed time.
We never know what'll happen.

174
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:00,326
No.

175
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:02,453
Sometimes, you seem like someone
being chased every single day.

176
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:05,456
You even plan your funeral
before going on a trip.

177
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:07,750
Huh!

178
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:10,503
What?

179
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:11,420
Unbelievable.

180
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,588
[intriguing music]

181
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:14,924
Is there some secret
you can't tell me?

182
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:17,593
Like you have debt
or some chronic illness?

183
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:21,847
Oh my, mother-in-law.

184
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,849
[tapping] It's because I'm a J
down to my bones.

185
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:25,935
Sorry, I'm a P down to my bones.

186
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,940
But who exactly is this mother-in-law
you keep desperately calling for?

187
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:35,569
In Gyeongsang-do,
they call a mother-in-law "sieomassi."

188
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,948
And a mother-in-law is supposed to be
the scariest person in the world,

189
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:41,367
but when things are even worse than that,

190
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:43,077
when you'd rather miss your mother-in-law,

191
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,579
my mom always says that.

192
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,748
She's probably calling for
her mother-in-law somewhere right now.

193
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:50,543
[Ha-min's mother] Oh my, mother-in-law.

194
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,587
[bright music]

195
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:02,138
Heave-ho.

196
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:06,559
[Ha-min's mother humming]

197
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:12,064
Whoosh!

198
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:16,318
Goodness, that's done.

199
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:18,737
[Ha-min's mother grunting]

200
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,039
Hmm.

201
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,834
How much do these cost these days?

202
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:36,172
{\an8}When my boy gets married,
I should get him one of these.

203
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,506
{\an8}[notification sound]

204
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:47,016
[ding-dong - doorbell]

205
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:49,018
[woman] Huh?

206
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:50,561
Who is it?

207
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:52,813
Oh, who is it?

208
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:55,483
- Who are you?
- [Ha-min's mother] Ah...

209
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:07,536
- Here.
- Oh, thank you.

210
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:12,124
- Eat up.
- Okay.

211
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,709
I'll call Oppa and...

212
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:14,710
No, don't.

213
00:13:14,793 --> 00:13:17,880
I had a wedding in Seoul,
so I stopped by for a bit.

214
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:20,424
I was so curious how you two were living.

215
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:25,304
- Thank you for the food.
- [Ha-min's mother responds]

216
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:38,859
Ah.

217
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:42,655
I've never tried this soup before,
but it's really delicious.

218
00:13:44,573 --> 00:13:46,367
It's Ha-min's favorite.

219
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:48,452
That boy,

220
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:51,539
when he feels a chill coming on,
or when his body starts aching,

221
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,582
this is the first thing he asks for.

222
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:57,086
Where are your parents?

223
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,464
If it's your first time eating this,
you must not be from Gyeongsang-do.

224
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:06,929
People usually don't like it
when I talk about this.

225
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:08,639
Why?

226
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:12,142
I don't have parents.

227
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,564
That's nothing strange.
My mom and dad are both dead too.

228
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:17,982
[calm music]

229
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:20,860
You've probably been buying
all your kimchi and soybean paste, right?

230
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:23,028
Store-bought stuff doesn't taste good.

231
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:24,572
I'll send you everything from now on.

232
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:29,201
That brat never eats any of it
even when I pack it for him.

233
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:31,370
This is good. This is good.

234
00:14:31,453 --> 00:14:32,788
[Ha-min's mother laughs]

235
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,876
Yeah, eat a lot.

236
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:50,306
[cheerful music]

237
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:52,766
[announcer] The New Year's countdown
will begin shortly.

238
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,268
Across the country,

239
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:57,146
many people have gathered
to watch the New Year's countdown.

240
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:59,857
I hope everyone here
achieves everything they wish for.

241
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,400
May they all come true.

242
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:03,277
[people] 10, 9,

243
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,655
8, 7, 6,

244
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:09,283
5, 4, 3,

245
00:15:09,366 --> 00:15:11,410
2, 1.

246
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:14,163
{\an8}[people cheering]

247
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:23,923
- [woman] Happy New Year.
- [man 1] Please step back a little.

248
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:24,924
Excuse me, excuse me.

249
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,592
- [man 2] Excuse me, yes, yes.
- [man 1] Excuse me.

250
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:28,135
Please move inside.
Please step back a little.

251
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,511
- Huh?
- [man 1] Thank you.

252
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:30,471
Thank you so much.

253
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:32,598
[people] Oh, what is this?
What's going on? What is it?

254
00:15:32,681 --> 00:15:33,599
[passerby 1] Oh!

255
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:35,267
- I think he's proposing.
- [murmuring]

256
00:15:37,853 --> 00:15:39,271
- Marry me.
- [people] Oh!

257
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:42,107
I won't just be your husband.
I'll be on your side forever.

258
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,817
[applause]

259
00:15:49,531 --> 00:15:51,075
But I have one condition.

260
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:53,535
Huh?

261
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:57,915
Your mother is alone in Busan.

262
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:00,334
Let's live with her.

263
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:04,713
You said you miss her every day.

264
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:09,385
No, I mean, that's true, but...

265
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:12,888
I always told you, Oppa.

266
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:15,557
My only insecurity is family.

267
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:18,227
No.

268
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:19,687
Why not?

269
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,897
Just... Just no.

270
00:16:25,776 --> 00:16:26,986
Then I can't either.

271
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:28,529
- Huh?
- [whispering]

272
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:29,530
[passersby] What? Is it over?

273
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:31,615
[passerby 2] What? Why won't she take the ring?

274
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:32,700
[woman] Marriage

275
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:37,663
is my only chance to have a family.

276
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:41,041
Find someone else.

277
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:43,335
[passersby] What?

278
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:44,878
Unbelievable. Oh my, oh my, oh my.

279
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:45,838
[passerby 3] Unbelievable.

280
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:47,006
[passerby 4] I'm embarrassed for him.

281
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,632
[murmuring]

282
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:52,428
[man 1] Hey, damn it.

283
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:54,221
Hey, you idiot.

284
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,598
You're whining when you're already blessed.

285
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:58,809
[man 1] Hey, what are you standing there for?

286
00:16:58,892 --> 00:17:00,394
[man 2] Hurry up and go after her
before you regret it.

287
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:02,104
- [passerby 5] That wasn't right.
- [man 1] Good grief.

288
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:03,689
[man 2] What are you really going to do?

289
00:17:03,772 --> 00:17:05,858
[calm music]

290
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:06,984
[door closes]

291
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:24,877
[spatula tapping]

292
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:37,806
Oh!

293
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:42,519
Dad.

294
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:44,354
[Ha-min's father] How do you know my face?

295
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:47,649
[hesitating] Oh, I saw you in photos.

296
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:49,151
[Ha-min's father] Is that so?

297
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,236
I look better in person, right?

298
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:53,280
Yeah.

299
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:55,074
Bring me some rice too. Let's eat.

300
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:56,241
- [Ha-min] Okay.
- Heave-ho.

301
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:00,996
You were upset
that Dad never appeared in your dreams, right?

302
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,083
Even if you never saw me,

303
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:06,335
I watched you grow up the whole time.

304
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:08,462
[Ha-min chuckles] Really?

305
00:18:08,545 --> 00:18:10,005
No, I wasn't upset.

306
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:13,258
But I've never eaten with you before,

307
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:15,094
so I don't know how much rice to give you.
Is this enough?

308
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:16,220
Yeah, that's enough.

309
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:17,679
- Sit down. Let's eat.
- [Ha-min] Okay.

310
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:33,529
{\an8}You're curious what that is, right?

311
00:18:35,572 --> 00:18:36,573
You can see it too, Dad?

312
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:40,869
When that number reaches zero,
your mom will die.

313
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:44,706
What?

314
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,377
Really?

315
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:54,466
Ha, isn't this way too cruel to me?

316
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:56,844
Don't you feel sorry for me?

317
00:18:57,719 --> 00:19:00,055
Who the hell is playing this joke on me?

318
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,014
Is it God?

319
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:03,976
Or is it you, Dad?

320
00:19:04,059 --> 00:19:05,561
[bowl placed down]

321
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:08,438
It's not God, and it's not me.

322
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:11,191
It's just your fate.

323
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:18,657
But fate can change.

324
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,616
You know that, right?

325
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,892
[door clicks]

326
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,271
[woman] What are you doing here?

327
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:52,774
[Ha-min] Oh, ahem. Are you going out now?

328
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,861
[woman] Don't tell me you slept here.

329
00:19:57,821 --> 00:19:58,655
Yeah.

330
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,410
Marriage aside,

331
00:20:03,493 --> 00:20:05,120
I'm not into men with crooked faces.

332
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:11,126
I have to go to work.

333
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:14,379
Come to my office later or something.

334
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:20,385
[door rattles]

335
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:23,263
[stomach growling]

336
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:27,976
[Ha-min] Ah...

337
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:29,603
{\an8}"Mom's Homemade Taste"

338
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,438
{\an8}"Momchan Kimchi"

339
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,232
{\an8}"Mom's Home Cooking"?

340
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,900
{\an8}[calm music]

341
00:20:34,983 --> 00:20:36,818
They all say their moms made it.

342
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:39,905
[clattering]

343
00:20:39,988 --> 00:20:41,281
[rustling]

344
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:56,630
[commotion]

345
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:04,554
Hey, my mom is sick today,
so she couldn't pack my lunch.

346
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:05,931
Share that with me.

347
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:06,848
[friend 1] Come on, damn it.

348
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:07,933
[friend 2] This punk is using his mom
as an excuse again.

349
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,685
Hey, I ran into your mom
at Jagalchi Market yesterday

350
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:10,978
- and said hi to her.
- [Ha-min] What are you talking about?

351
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:12,604
Hey, my mom really is sick right now.

352
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:13,689
[friend 2] Ah...

353
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:14,856
- What, she's always...
- [friend 1] Eat.

354
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,108
- Hey, just eat this.
- [friend 1] It's fine, it's fine.

355
00:21:16,191 --> 00:21:17,609
- Eat it all.
- Hey, just eat it with your fingers.

356
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:18,777
[friend 1] My mom makes great gimbap.

357
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:21,947
[friend 2] Hey, tell your mom
to open a Gimbap Hell.

358
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:24,533
[friend 1] It's not Gimbap Hell,
it's Gimbap Heaven, idiot.

359
00:21:24,616 --> 00:21:25,701
Hey, listen.

360
00:21:27,202 --> 00:21:30,747
Every time you eat food your mom made,
the number counts down by one.

361
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,458
And when it reaches zero,
your mom dies.

362
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:34,376
What do you think you'd do?

363
00:21:34,459 --> 00:21:35,836
Your mom doesn't know?

364
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:36,962
No.

365
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:38,588
Then of course you shouldn't tell her.

366
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:39,840
Listen.

367
00:21:39,923 --> 00:21:41,883
What if your mom starts worrying
about something like that

368
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:44,136
and ends up getting cancer
or some other illness?

369
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:45,387
Right, right.

370
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,514
I'd avoid it on my own
without telling her too.

371
00:21:48,056 --> 00:21:50,475
Even if you told her,
would your mom believe you?

372
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:51,393
Even if she did,

373
00:21:51,476 --> 00:21:53,729
what kind of mother in the world
would stop feeding her child

374
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:54,730
because she's afraid of dying?

375
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:58,734
Hey, but just imagining it is painful.

376
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:02,988
I mean, living in the same house
as your mom,

377
00:22:03,071 --> 00:22:04,823
but not being able to eat her food?

378
00:22:04,906 --> 00:22:06,408
Or maybe not?

379
00:22:06,491 --> 00:22:08,577
Oh, no, wait. That's not it.

380
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,370
Hey, you could just go out and buy food.

381
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:12,414
That would actually be awesome.

382
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:14,458
[friend 1] You're right.
That would seriously be awesome.

383
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:15,542
[friend 2] Exactly.

384
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:18,003
[Ha-min's mother] No,
I need to go home and cook.

385
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:19,546
[Ha-min] Come on.

386
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:21,590
[Ha-min's mother] Where are we going?

387
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:23,175
[Ha-min] There is somewhere.

388
00:22:23,258 --> 00:22:24,217
[Ha-min's mother] What is with you today?

389
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:25,552
[Ha-min] Seriously, come on.

390
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:27,637
- [Ha-min's mother] Goodness.
- [Ha-min] Come on.

391
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:28,889
[Ha-min's mother] Seriously.

392
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:31,433
My goodness.

393
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:33,101
Mom, please!

394
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,102
I said I don't want to.

395
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,604
Please, please, please, please.

396
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:37,773
[Ha-min's mother] Hey! Seriously.

397
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:40,317
Why do you keep wanting
to eat out these days?

398
00:22:40,942 --> 00:22:42,277
We're already tight on money.

399
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:44,613
{\an8}They're asking us to raise the rent,

400
00:22:44,696 --> 00:22:46,406
{\an8}and we've used up all your dad's
insurance money too.

401
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:48,617
We need every penny
for your college tuition.

402
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:49,534
Ah!

403
00:22:50,452 --> 00:22:51,536
Mom.

404
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:54,539
Just one day. Just today.

405
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:55,457
Let's go.

406
00:22:57,417 --> 00:22:58,251
[woman/TV] If you follow the fish,

407
00:22:58,335 --> 00:23:00,629
you end up at places
that are great for taking photos.

408
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:01,713
[cheerful music]

409
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,215
- [TV playing]
- [door opens]

410
00:23:03,298 --> 00:23:05,342
- Did you eat?
- [Ha-min] I bought something on the way.

411
00:23:06,009 --> 00:23:07,677
- [door opens]
- Did you eat?

412
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:09,387
[Ha-min] Ah, I don't have an appetite.

413
00:23:10,722 --> 00:23:12,265
- [Ha-min's mother] Did you eat?
- I feel nauseous.

414
00:23:13,809 --> 00:23:14,643
Did you eat?

415
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:16,770
No, it's fine.
Just watching you eat fills me up.

416
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:18,980
Bullshit. Eat with Mom.

417
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,149
No, no. You eat first.
I have something to do.

418
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:29,825
[Ha-min/narration] To protect Mom,

419
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:32,077
I have to leave her.

420
00:23:33,537 --> 00:23:35,205
As long as I keep my head straight,

421
00:23:35,914 --> 00:23:37,332
I can change fate too.

422
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:40,377
[bright music]

423
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:42,295
First, I need to leave home.

424
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:46,591
No matter what,
I'll go to college in Seoul.

425
00:23:55,433 --> 00:23:57,853
Goodness, Eun-sil.

426
00:23:57,936 --> 00:23:59,771
You're going to burn a hole through it.
Eat first.

427
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:02,399
There are plenty of good universities
in Busan too.

428
00:24:03,859 --> 00:24:06,361
If you run off to Seoul,
what about your mom?

429
00:24:07,571 --> 00:24:09,156
Why do you only think of yourself?

430
00:24:09,239 --> 00:24:10,198
Huh?

431
00:24:11,032 --> 00:24:12,701
Other parents are desperate
because they can't send their kids to Seoul.

432
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:14,369
What's with you, Mom?

433
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:17,706
Then,

434
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:19,624
what's your dream?

435
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:20,709
Dream?

436
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:22,878
To die of natural causes.

437
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:24,421
What nonsense.

438
00:24:24,504 --> 00:24:27,883
How can a young man's dream
be so tiny?

439
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:29,467
Good grief.

440
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:32,387
Do you think you'll do well in Seoul?

441
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:35,182
- Oh my, mother-in-law.
- [Eun-sil] Ha...

442
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:37,851
Like you always say,
what could be scarier than a mother-in-law?

443
00:24:38,393 --> 00:24:40,478
Goodness, you little brat.

444
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,189
All talk, aren't you?

445
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:44,107
Come on, let's eat.

446
00:24:48,236 --> 00:24:49,571
[calm music]

447
00:24:49,654 --> 00:24:50,572
Mm.

448
00:25:01,416 --> 00:25:02,500
[Ha-min sighs softly]

449
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:05,253
[Ha-min] So...

450
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:08,632
I don't think I can live with my mom.

451
00:25:14,137 --> 00:25:17,265
Now I understand why
you kept worrying about things in advance.

452
00:25:18,683 --> 00:25:19,517
Right?

453
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:26,274
You must have had a lot
on your mind all this time.

454
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:33,615
[Ha-min] Thank you.

455
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:37,285
But, Oppa...

456
00:25:37,869 --> 00:25:39,704
[calm music]

457
00:25:41,248 --> 00:25:42,958
You expect me to believe that?

458
00:25:43,583 --> 00:25:44,542
Huh?

459
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:46,336
[woman] You can't live with her
because you're afraid she'll die

460
00:25:46,419 --> 00:25:47,545
if you eat her food?

461
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,297
Does that make sense?

462
00:25:49,881 --> 00:25:52,801
You're not cursed with worries.
Worrying is your actual fate.

463
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:55,136
Worrying is my fate?

464
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:56,179
Forget it.

465
00:25:56,972 --> 00:25:58,932
I don't want to get in the way
of your life anymore.

466
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:01,226
A coffin is a single room anyway.

467
00:26:01,309 --> 00:26:02,560
Let's each go find our own happiness.

468
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,946
[Eun-sil] He's always been selfish.

469
00:26:13,029 --> 00:26:15,657
What's so great about a selfish kid?

470
00:26:16,950 --> 00:26:18,410
Don't worry about me.

471
00:26:18,493 --> 00:26:20,495
A widow is more comfortable living alone.

472
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:22,831
I'm not comfortable with that.

473
00:26:23,540 --> 00:26:24,416
[Eun-sil] Ryeo-eun.

474
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:27,627
Instead of being your mother-in-law,

475
00:26:27,711 --> 00:26:31,381
I'll just be your mom. Your mom.

476
00:26:31,464 --> 00:26:32,549
[Eun-sil chuckles softly]

477
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:44,769
[phone notification]

478
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:03,747
{\an8}- Here.
- [video playing noisily]

479
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,792
{\an8}[friend 1] Huh? Isn't this lady
the godmother of chicken feet?

480
00:27:07,876 --> 00:27:09,210
- I'll give you lots.
- I'll pile it on!

481
00:27:11,212 --> 00:27:12,922
Ha, why would I show you?

482
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:14,549
Ah, Team Leader.

483
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:18,762
As you know,
this place only keeps using Sanhae soju.

484
00:27:18,845 --> 00:27:20,388
Even when we visit,
they don't give us a single glance.

485
00:27:20,472 --> 00:27:22,849
An order came down from the chairman.

486
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:26,686
He wants to use this restaurant owner
as an advertising model.

487
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:30,065
[friend 2] Ah, we can't even get them
to accept our alcohol.
Casting her as a model makes no sense.

488
00:27:30,148 --> 00:27:31,358
[friend 1] Ah, Team Leader, well...

489
00:27:31,441 --> 00:27:34,402
There's also that Turkish jeon place next door
with the owner who swears really well.

490
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:36,988
Even if this is our territory,

491
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:38,239
casting someone for an ad is a bit...

492
00:27:38,323 --> 00:27:40,867
Oh-ho, the slaves are talking?

493
00:27:42,577 --> 00:27:43,995
It's an order from headquarters,
so there must be something to it.

494
00:27:44,079 --> 00:27:47,040
You know, like a bonus
or a promotion, huh?

495
00:27:47,874 --> 00:27:49,042
I'll give it a try.

496
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,587
Well, what is life anyway?
It's all or nothing.

497
00:27:53,171 --> 00:27:54,964
- Hey, that will never work, man.
- [friend 2] What's with you?

498
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:56,633
I'll try it.

499
00:27:57,592 --> 00:27:59,677
I'll handle it myself.

500
00:27:59,761 --> 00:28:00,762
Coming soon.

501
00:28:01,596 --> 00:28:02,430
[friend 1] Wow.

502
00:28:04,724 --> 00:28:06,059
What's gotten into him all of a sudden?

503
00:28:06,142 --> 00:28:07,852
Apparently, they really broke up this time.

504
00:28:08,645 --> 00:28:10,063
Love and marriage are both done for.

505
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,524
Ah, I see.

506
00:28:13,274 --> 00:28:15,693
- [intriguing music]
- Hello, Hanryang is here!

507
00:28:15,777 --> 00:28:17,654
[owner] Oh my, oh my.
Please leave.

508
00:28:17,737 --> 00:28:19,072
[Ha-min] Ah...

509
00:28:23,868 --> 00:28:25,370
- [owner] Go, go, leave!
- [Ha-min] Oh...

510
00:28:25,453 --> 00:28:27,038
[owner] Hurry up and go. Hurry.

511
00:28:27,122 --> 00:28:29,207
- [Ha-min] Oh, hello.
- [owner] Goodness, I'm so sick of this.

512
00:28:29,290 --> 00:28:30,208
[Ha-min] Please take this...

513
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:31,543
Oh, gosh.

514
00:28:31,626 --> 00:28:33,461
- [owner] Please, please just go!
- [Ha-min] Ah...

515
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,801
[humming]

516
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:49,436
Here, table two.

517
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:50,478
[employee] Okay.

518
00:28:51,271 --> 00:28:52,814
Ah, yes, thank you.

519
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,734
Your chicken feet are here.

520
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:57,318
Enjoy your meal.

521
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:58,903
Please enjoy, yes.

522
00:29:03,158 --> 00:29:04,409
- Ah, seriously!
- [Ha-min] Ah!

523
00:29:04,492 --> 00:29:05,493
Is this what you call an apple?

524
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:07,328
What a waste, seriously.

525
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:09,247
- No, this is...
- You have to cut off the stem first.

526
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:11,416
- Oh my goodness.
- [customers cheering]

527
00:29:11,499 --> 00:29:13,293
[customers reacting excitedly]

528
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:16,504
Now, watch carefully.

529
00:29:16,588 --> 00:29:19,090
- Now I'm making the honey drink!
- [customers cheering]

530
00:29:19,674 --> 00:29:21,009
Say "ah."

531
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:29,184
Ahem.

532
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:36,941
[Ha-min groaning]

533
00:29:38,902 --> 00:29:39,986
[phone buzzing]

534
00:30:04,219 --> 00:30:05,887
Ah, ugh.

535
00:30:07,013 --> 00:30:08,056
Ah...

536
00:30:24,697 --> 00:30:26,699
[calm music]

537
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:50,932
Ah, owner, don't you have any perilla leaves?

538
00:30:52,267 --> 00:30:53,518
[owner] Ah, these days,
perilla leaves are as expensive as gold.

539
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:54,727
[employee] Your meat is here.

540
00:30:54,811 --> 00:30:56,354
Oh, sorry about that, sir.

541
00:30:57,897 --> 00:30:58,773
Should we go somewhere else?

542
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:01,734
The meat is already on the grill.
Where would we go? Just eat, Oppa.

543
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:04,362
It's okay, Oppa.

544
00:31:04,445 --> 00:31:06,197
- I like lettuce too.
- No, no.

545
00:31:06,281 --> 00:31:07,532
[Ryeo-eun] Ah...

546
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:15,999
[Ha-min] Goodness.

547
00:31:16,791 --> 00:31:18,334
The meat is grilled nicely.

548
00:31:20,628 --> 00:31:21,504
Ah.

549
00:31:22,463 --> 00:31:23,298
Ah.

550
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:27,135
It's just perilla leaves, damn it.

551
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:29,262
Let's eat.

552
00:31:37,145 --> 00:31:38,605
Did the owner go back to basics?

553
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:41,232
They've been serving perilla leaves well lately.

554
00:31:45,653 --> 00:31:46,988
- [door closes]
- [door lock sound]

555
00:31:47,822 --> 00:31:48,823
[door lock sound]

556
00:32:10,678 --> 00:32:11,512
[beep]

557
00:32:26,945 --> 00:32:28,029
[ding-dong - doorbell]

558
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:38,122
What about dinner? Did you eat?

559
00:32:38,706 --> 00:32:39,624
Ah, not yet.

560
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:45,380
- [door closes]
- [door lock sound]

561
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:48,591
Oppa.

562
00:32:49,175 --> 00:32:51,928
I saw on the news
that someone did a survey.

563
00:32:52,011 --> 00:32:54,931
Do you know what ranked first
for when people decide to break up?

564
00:32:57,934 --> 00:32:59,727
When they can't stand
watching the other person eat.

565
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:03,982
I still want to watch you eat.

566
00:33:11,197 --> 00:33:12,156
I love you.

567
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,324
[Ryeo-eun] Me too.

568
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:24,043
[Ha-min] Wow.

569
00:33:24,585 --> 00:33:26,170
Have you tried beef soup before?

570
00:33:26,254 --> 00:33:27,839
- [Ryeo-eun] Yes.
- [intriguing music]

571
00:33:27,922 --> 00:33:29,507
No.

572
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:31,968
Huh? Then how are you going to make it?

573
00:33:34,137 --> 00:33:35,430
- [Eun-sil] Like this.
- [Ryeo-eun] Okay.

574
00:33:42,603 --> 00:33:46,357
Ha-min has always been frail,
ever since he was little.

575
00:33:46,441 --> 00:33:49,402
Whenever he gets sick,
boil him a pot of this,

576
00:33:49,485 --> 00:33:50,528
and he'll get better quickly.

577
00:33:51,487 --> 00:33:52,864
[both laughing]

578
00:33:52,947 --> 00:33:54,532
- Look, look. It's done, right?
- [Ryeo-eun] Oh!

579
00:34:06,419 --> 00:34:07,420
Huh?

580
00:34:11,841 --> 00:34:12,800
Mm...

581
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:14,677
Mm.

582
00:34:21,225 --> 00:34:22,602
Wow.

583
00:34:22,685 --> 00:34:24,062
This is really the taste.

584
00:34:24,145 --> 00:34:26,105
This is seriously delicious.

585
00:34:26,189 --> 00:34:27,398
This is the taste.

586
00:34:27,482 --> 00:34:28,483
Soul.

587
00:34:29,233 --> 00:34:30,485
No, it's really good.

588
00:34:34,113 --> 00:34:35,448
Hmph, I made it exactly the same.

589
00:34:36,324 --> 00:34:37,158
Huh?

590
00:34:38,659 --> 00:34:40,328
Do you know why I became a dietitian?

591
00:34:40,995 --> 00:34:42,080
Why?

592
00:34:42,663 --> 00:34:45,958
They say a lack of something
isn't a flaw, but a possibility.

593
00:34:47,001 --> 00:34:50,505
I grew up without eating my mom's cooking,
so I wanted to cook warm meals like that.

594
00:34:54,342 --> 00:34:55,176
And, Oppa...

595
00:34:57,011 --> 00:34:58,971
I've thought about it,

596
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,850
and I think I was being selfish.

597
00:35:06,687 --> 00:35:07,939
It's because I grew up hungry.

598
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:10,024
It's because I'm twisted.

599
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:13,194
It's because I'm not good enough.

600
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:16,322
No, no, no, no.

601
00:35:17,156 --> 00:35:19,117
My mom and I...

602
00:35:19,992 --> 00:35:21,869
We've each lived separately for too long,

603
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:24,664
so I think living together
would be a little difficult.

604
00:35:26,040 --> 00:35:28,835
Instead, let's go down to Busan often

605
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:30,128
and eat galbi and raw fish.

606
00:35:30,211 --> 00:35:31,546
And fish cake skewers?

607
00:35:31,629 --> 00:35:32,880
Huh? How did you know?

608
00:35:33,506 --> 00:35:36,217
Fish cake skewers, seed hotteok,
bibim glass noodles.

609
00:35:36,884 --> 00:35:39,262
Come, look, and buy!

610
00:35:39,345 --> 00:35:40,263
[Ha-min laughing]

611
00:35:42,473 --> 00:35:44,350
[light music]

612
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:53,234
[phone notification]

613
00:35:54,902 --> 00:35:55,945
[chopsticks clacking]

614
00:36:20,928 --> 00:36:21,762
[water running]

615
00:36:52,710 --> 00:36:53,878
It's so delicious.

616
00:36:56,714 --> 00:36:58,257
How did you know about these soybean leaves?

617
00:36:58,341 --> 00:36:59,967
Only people from Gyeongsang-do know these.

618
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:01,594
You know I like perilla leaves, right?

619
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:05,473
I don't just love perilla leaves.
I love every leaf on Earth.

620
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:06,974
And did you forget I'm a dietitian?

621
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:08,392
What food from Korea would I not know?

622
00:37:08,476 --> 00:37:11,020
Wow, look who thinks she's Dae Jang-geum.

623
00:37:11,103 --> 00:37:12,855
- I'm really breaking up with you.
- I love you.

624
00:37:12,939 --> 00:37:13,981
Make this for me every day after we get married.

625
00:37:15,733 --> 00:37:16,984
Isn't it spicy?

626
00:37:17,068 --> 00:37:18,236
It's not spicy. It's so good.

627
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:21,030
[Ha-min laughing]

628
00:37:21,864 --> 00:37:24,575
{\an8}[Ha-min] But why aren't there
any jeonse listings for us?

629
00:37:24,659 --> 00:37:26,994
Should we just pool everything we have
and buy a place?

630
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:32,458
[Ryeo-eun] Ha... What's wrong
with paying monthly rent?

631
00:37:33,334 --> 00:37:34,752
Let's not be too greedy.

632
00:37:34,835 --> 00:37:36,420
What did you say your dream was?

633
00:37:37,546 --> 00:37:38,422
To die of natural causes.

634
00:37:39,090 --> 00:37:41,968
Then if you want to die of natural causes,
at least get a proper endoscopy.

635
00:37:42,510 --> 00:37:45,221
You've never once had
your company health checkup, right?

636
00:37:45,304 --> 00:37:48,474
What if they suddenly tell me
I'm going to die? I'm scared.

637
00:37:48,557 --> 00:37:50,601
Oh my, mother-in-law.

638
00:37:50,685 --> 00:37:51,894
[Ha-min humming]

639
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:53,646
Good grief!

640
00:37:53,729 --> 00:37:54,605
[Ha-min chuckles softly]

641
00:37:55,356 --> 00:37:56,774
- [Ha-min] Look at this.
- [Ryeo-eun] Okay.

642
00:37:56,857 --> 00:37:58,276
How much is it?

643
00:37:58,359 --> 00:37:59,777
- Whoa!
- [Ha-min] Ah...

644
00:37:59,860 --> 00:38:03,155
[Ryeo-eun] I made soybean leaves for him,
and he said they tasted just like yours.

645
00:38:03,239 --> 00:38:05,116
- I guess I'm pretty good at cooking too...
- Is that so?

646
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:08,703
Then I guess you don't need me anymore.

647
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:10,454
[Ryeo-eun] Pardon?

648
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:13,624
No, never mind.
I'm here to clean right now. We'll talk later...

649
00:38:13,708 --> 00:38:15,251
[Ryeo-eun] Okay, Mom.
I'll talk to you later.

650
00:38:17,128 --> 00:38:18,504
- [thud - vacuum cleaner]
- [heavy music]

651
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:20,798
Ah...

652
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:23,718
Ugh!

653
00:38:25,511 --> 00:38:26,595
Ah...

654
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:29,348
Ah...

655
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:39,734
[Ha-min breathing urgently]

656
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:42,611
Excuse me! Um...

657
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:44,822
Where is the operating room?

658
00:38:44,905 --> 00:38:46,032
- [staff] Third floor.
- [Ha-min] Ah.

659
00:38:51,996 --> 00:38:54,332
Oh, you're here? That must've been hard.

660
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:55,541
Auntie.

661
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:58,002
Since when was Mom feeling unwell?

662
00:38:58,085 --> 00:38:59,211
Why is she suddenly having surgery?

663
00:38:59,795 --> 00:39:01,005
I don't know.

664
00:39:01,088 --> 00:39:02,840
Your mom isn't the type
to tell me anything.

665
00:39:04,925 --> 00:39:06,260
A few days ago,

666
00:39:06,344 --> 00:39:09,472
she said, "Unnie, no matter how much cider I drink,
I can't digest anything."

667
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:12,892
Goodness, she's so foolish. Seriously.

668
00:39:14,268 --> 00:39:15,436
Ah...

669
00:39:35,289 --> 00:39:38,376
When that number reaches zero,
your mom will die.

670
00:39:38,459 --> 00:39:40,461
[calm music]

671
00:39:44,173 --> 00:39:45,466
[Ha-min breathing heavily]

672
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:08,614
[sniffling]

673
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:46,402
[Ha-min] Ha...

674
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:02,543
{\an8}[phone ringing]

675
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:06,839
Yeah, what about Mom?

676
00:41:09,425 --> 00:41:11,010
[Ha-min's aunt] The doctor said

677
00:41:12,636 --> 00:41:14,680
they removed 80 percent of her pancreas.

678
00:41:15,556 --> 00:41:18,559
She can't eat meat anymore.
What are you going to do?

679
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:22,730
[Ha-min] Mom never liked meat anyway.

680
00:41:23,689 --> 00:41:24,815
[Ha-min's aunt] That's a relief.

681
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:29,236
Oh, Ha-min, you're not going back right away, are you?

682
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:33,574
I need to step out for a bit,
so stay by your mom's side.

683
00:41:34,116 --> 00:41:35,117
[Ha-min] Okay.

684
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:39,705
[Ha-min's aunt] Goodness,
how am I supposed to live without a son?

685
00:41:40,414 --> 00:41:43,751
Your son was crying and making a fuss
at the crack of dawn.

686
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:46,921
Sigh.

687
00:42:01,894 --> 00:42:04,313
Why do you look so angry?

688
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:08,692
Are you mad because you had to come down here
when you're busy?

689
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:09,735
Ha...

690
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:13,989
Where did you spend all the money I sent you?

691
00:42:14,949 --> 00:42:15,908
Are you gambling behind my back?

692
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:20,913
Why didn't you go to the hospital regularly?
What were you doing?

693
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:25,125
I really thought you were dying...

694
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:26,752
I'm sorry.

695
00:42:28,420 --> 00:42:29,630
Stop scolding me now.

696
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:33,259
How could I spend the money you gave me?

697
00:42:33,342 --> 00:42:36,554
I saved every bit of it
to help you when you get married.

698
00:42:38,222 --> 00:42:39,223
Mom.

699
00:42:41,058 --> 00:42:42,601
I'm not getting married.

700
00:42:43,352 --> 00:42:45,187
No, I can't because of you.

701
00:42:45,271 --> 00:42:47,898
So don't make me worry about you, okay?

702
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:50,401
Okay. Ah, well...

703
00:42:50,484 --> 00:42:52,236
When I get discharged tomorrow,

704
00:42:52,319 --> 00:42:54,530
I'll go home

705
00:42:54,613 --> 00:42:55,447
and make you some side dishes, so take them with you.

706
00:42:55,531 --> 00:42:57,491
I'll make your favorite beef soup and...

707
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:58,826
Everything you make

708
00:42:59,535 --> 00:43:00,786
is salty and spicy.

709
00:43:03,163 --> 00:43:04,331
Buying food is much better.

710
00:43:06,917 --> 00:43:09,253
I really can't stand looking at you.

711
00:43:23,017 --> 00:43:25,019
[heavy music]

712
00:43:41,410 --> 00:43:42,369
[knife hits cutting board]

713
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:48,334
[chopping]

714
00:43:49,877 --> 00:43:50,919
[door clicks]

715
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:54,715
- [door thuds]
- [Ha-min] Huh?

716
00:43:55,549 --> 00:43:56,550
Goodness.

717
00:43:57,426 --> 00:43:58,552
What is all this?

718
00:43:59,386 --> 00:44:01,472
Have even just one spoonful before you go.

719
00:44:01,555 --> 00:44:03,140
Unless you want to see your mother die.

720
00:44:03,807 --> 00:44:04,975
I'm late for school.

721
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:06,560
[Eun-sil] Don't go to school.

722
00:44:06,644 --> 00:44:07,853
Mom will call them.

723
00:44:09,271 --> 00:44:10,856
What are you talking about?
I'll come back and eat it later.

724
00:44:12,274 --> 00:44:15,194
Was the lunch I packed for your picnic yesterday good?

725
00:44:21,950 --> 00:44:24,995
Are you afraid you'll die like your brother

726
00:44:26,747 --> 00:44:30,417
if you eat the food Mom makes?

727
00:44:30,501 --> 00:44:32,169
Is that why you keep avoiding it,
throwing it away, and not eating it?

728
00:44:32,252 --> 00:44:33,712
Damn it, that's not it...

729
00:44:57,444 --> 00:44:59,363
Mom, you really can't see that number?

730
00:44:59,446 --> 00:45:01,198
When that number runs out, you'll die.

731
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:03,909
Number?

732
00:45:04,618 --> 00:45:05,953
What number?

733
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:09,581
Where is there a number?

734
00:45:10,582 --> 00:45:12,126
Where? Huh?

735
00:45:13,293 --> 00:45:14,461
Where is the number?

736
00:45:15,671 --> 00:45:16,505
Where?

737
00:45:20,634 --> 00:45:23,554
Ha-min, please come to your senses.

738
00:45:30,144 --> 00:45:31,186
{\an8}Or...

739
00:45:31,979 --> 00:45:34,898
{\an8}Do you want to go see a psychiatrist with Mom?

740
00:45:36,275 --> 00:45:37,943
People say psychiatry isn't something
to be ashamed of these days.

741
00:45:38,026 --> 00:45:39,653
- My friend's daughter...
- [table bangs]

742
00:45:41,989 --> 00:45:43,449
Do I look mentally ill to you?

743
00:45:45,242 --> 00:45:46,368
You go.

744
00:45:52,791 --> 00:45:55,335
[door opens and shuts]

745
00:45:55,419 --> 00:45:58,380
[doctor] Well, he suddenly lost
his older brother,

746
00:45:58,464 --> 00:46:00,090
so he must be having a very hard time emotionally.

747
00:46:00,966 --> 00:46:02,968
{\an8}After something like that happens,

748
00:46:03,051 --> 00:46:04,303
{\an8}because of post-traumatic stress disorder,

749
00:46:04,386 --> 00:46:07,764
people can hear ringing in their ears
or see things that aren't there.

750
00:46:07,848 --> 00:46:11,518
It's the mind trying to protect itself.

751
00:46:11,602 --> 00:46:13,145
It's a natural reaction.

752
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:15,439
Once enough time passes,

753
00:46:15,522 --> 00:46:17,941
everything will be all right.

754
00:46:20,152 --> 00:46:22,404
Is work bearable?

755
00:46:22,488 --> 00:46:23,447
[Ha-min] Yeah.

756
00:46:24,031 --> 00:46:25,532
Is your boss giving you hell?

757
00:46:26,366 --> 00:46:27,242
No.

758
00:46:28,243 --> 00:46:29,828
Do you want more rice?

759
00:46:32,206 --> 00:46:33,332
No, I'm done eating.

760
00:46:34,374 --> 00:46:35,709
It's almost time for my train.

761
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:44,051
[Eun-sil] I know you're busy,

762
00:46:44,843 --> 00:46:47,387
but who else would I chat with besides you?

763
00:46:48,388 --> 00:46:51,058
You have Auntie, don't you? I'm going.

764
00:47:45,779 --> 00:47:47,781
[Ryeo-eun] You haven't even had dinner.
What were you doing?

765
00:47:49,616 --> 00:47:51,159
Ta-da.

766
00:47:51,243 --> 00:47:54,621
This is Gyemisae ramyeon,
a new recipe I developed.

767
00:47:54,705 --> 00:47:56,039
[Ha-min] What is that? Gyemisae?

768
00:47:56,123 --> 00:47:57,040
[Ryeo-eun] Egg, seaweed, and shrimp.

769
00:47:57,124 --> 00:47:59,084
- Hurry and try it.
- [Ha-min] Ah.

770
00:47:59,167 --> 00:48:00,502
- Hey, damn.
- [Ryeo-eun] It's hot.

771
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:02,713
[Ha-min blowing]

772
00:48:09,177 --> 00:48:10,971
Wow, this is killer.

773
00:48:19,479 --> 00:48:21,440
[mysterious sound effect]

774
00:48:22,357 --> 00:48:24,735
[dark music]

775
00:48:24,818 --> 00:48:25,986
[chopsticks clatter]

776
00:48:30,157 --> 00:48:31,158
Fuck.

777
00:48:31,825 --> 00:48:33,160
Oppa.

778
00:48:34,703 --> 00:48:36,121
Where did you get the kimchi?

779
00:48:39,625 --> 00:48:40,751
I bought it.

780
00:48:40,834 --> 00:48:41,793
You bought it?

781
00:48:43,003 --> 00:48:43,837
[Ryeo-eun] Yeah.

782
00:48:46,214 --> 00:48:47,507
My mom didn't give it to you?

783
00:48:50,594 --> 00:48:51,678
How did you know?

784
00:48:53,805 --> 00:48:56,350
So if you really eat something
your mom made, you see something?

785
00:48:56,433 --> 00:48:58,727
You can see that number behind me?

786
00:49:00,312 --> 00:49:01,521
Was this a test?

787
00:49:02,147 --> 00:49:02,981
No.

788
00:49:04,358 --> 00:49:05,359
That's not what this was...

789
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:09,404
You didn't believe me.

790
00:49:10,822 --> 00:49:12,491
You don't care if my mom dies.

791
00:49:12,574 --> 00:49:15,243
Oppa, why would you say it like that?

792
00:49:15,869 --> 00:49:18,205
Maybe it looks like a joke to you,

793
00:49:18,872 --> 00:49:20,332
but do you know what it's like

794
00:49:20,415 --> 00:49:22,042
to live your whole life anxious
because of that damn number?

795
00:49:23,710 --> 00:49:24,711
Did you ever think about me?

796
00:49:25,587 --> 00:49:26,713
Okay.

797
00:49:26,797 --> 00:49:28,548
Oppa, okay, so...

798
00:49:32,135 --> 00:49:33,053
[door opens]

799
00:49:34,262 --> 00:49:35,555
[door slams]

800
00:49:36,181 --> 00:49:37,766
[customers talking]

801
00:49:46,858 --> 00:49:48,110
Ah, ha...

802
00:50:11,758 --> 00:50:13,760
[calm music]

803
00:50:33,655 --> 00:50:34,823
[soft sigh]

804
00:50:46,710 --> 00:50:48,462
- Ha...
- [dial tone]

805
00:51:00,557 --> 00:51:01,892
[Eun-sil] Oh, Ha-min.

806
00:51:03,185 --> 00:51:04,519
Did you get back safely?

807
00:51:05,395 --> 00:51:06,480
Did you eat?

808
00:51:07,564 --> 00:51:08,899
[sobbing]

809
00:51:11,818 --> 00:51:12,652
Why?

810
00:51:14,154 --> 00:51:15,155
Mom.

811
00:51:33,215 --> 00:51:34,508
Mom.

812
00:51:37,677 --> 00:51:39,304
[Ha-min sobbing]

813
00:51:44,017 --> 00:51:45,227
Mom.

814
00:51:47,729 --> 00:51:49,022
[Ha-min crying]

815
00:52:26,393 --> 00:52:28,061
[cheerful music]

816
00:52:28,144 --> 00:52:30,522
[narrator] Even when you're alone,
this moment is the best.

817
00:52:31,064 --> 00:52:34,234
The one secret that breaks
the loneliness of drinking alone.

818
00:52:36,903 --> 00:52:39,281
{\an8}After living a while,
I learned somaek beats connections.

819
00:52:40,282 --> 00:52:41,408
[narrator] Hanryang.

820
00:52:42,409 --> 00:52:43,660
Ah!

821
00:52:43,743 --> 00:52:46,037
[employees] Wow! Whoa!

822
00:52:46,121 --> 00:52:46,997
[employee 1] Jung Ha-min!

823
00:52:47,080 --> 00:52:49,082
[employees cheering]

824
00:52:51,293 --> 00:52:52,377
[friend 1] Jung Ha-min!

825
00:52:52,460 --> 00:52:53,628
Wow, you really pulled it off.

826
00:52:53,712 --> 00:52:55,046
[friends] Wow, damn.

827
00:52:55,130 --> 00:52:56,339
Yap!

828
00:52:56,423 --> 00:52:57,924
They say it's hard to change
people's taste in soju?

829
00:52:58,800 --> 00:53:01,094
Yap! Who says that?

830
00:53:01,928 --> 00:53:03,054
Yap!

831
00:53:03,138 --> 00:53:04,264
Who said that?

832
00:53:05,807 --> 00:53:08,101
- Shall we toast?
- [employees cheering]

833
00:53:08,184 --> 00:53:10,020
Change it! Change it!

834
00:53:10,103 --> 00:53:12,772
[employees] Change everything to Hanryang!

835
00:53:12,856 --> 00:53:14,524
[employees cheering]

836
00:53:14,608 --> 00:53:16,067
[commotion]

837
00:53:17,110 --> 00:53:18,111
[Ha-min] Blech! [coughing]

838
00:53:18,194 --> 00:53:19,696
- [friend 1] Hey, hey, damn.
- [woman] What the hell?

839
00:53:19,779 --> 00:53:21,573
- [friend 1] Huh? Sorry, sorry.
- [Ha-min] Oh, I'm sorry.

840
00:53:21,656 --> 00:53:22,866
- [friend 1] Sorry.
- [Ha-min] I'm sorry.

841
00:53:22,949 --> 00:53:24,284
- [friend 1] Sorry.
- [friend 2] Ah, what's wrong with you?

842
00:53:24,367 --> 00:53:26,036
- [Ha-min] Ugh.
- [friend 1/laughing] This bastard is such a lightweight.

843
00:53:26,119 --> 00:53:27,996
- [Ha-min] Ah, what's wrong with me?
- [friend 1] Sorry.

844
00:53:28,079 --> 00:53:29,915
- Sorry.
- [friend 2] He drank all by himself.

845
00:53:29,998 --> 00:53:31,291
- [Ha-min coughing]
- [friends laughing]

846
00:53:31,374 --> 00:53:32,375
[Ha-min] Ugh.

847
00:53:33,543 --> 00:53:34,794
- Ow.
- [friend 2] Good grief.

848
00:53:36,171 --> 00:53:38,256
Hey, what about Ryeo-eun?

849
00:53:38,965 --> 00:53:40,258
Are you really done with her?

850
00:53:41,301 --> 00:53:42,552
What did you fight about?

851
00:53:42,636 --> 00:53:44,554
Ha... I don't know.

852
00:53:45,305 --> 00:53:46,890
Hey, man.

853
00:53:46,973 --> 00:53:48,558
How can you only think about yourself?

854
00:53:48,642 --> 00:53:50,310
This guy really only thinks about himself.

855
00:53:50,393 --> 00:53:51,645
[friend 2] Tsk, tsk.

856
00:53:54,105 --> 00:53:55,899
My taxi's here. I'm leaving first.

857
00:53:55,982 --> 00:53:56,858
[friends] Okay, yeah.

858
00:53:56,942 --> 00:53:58,234
- Go on.
- [friend 2] Get home safe.

859
00:54:00,111 --> 00:54:01,154
[friend 2] Sigh.

860
00:54:06,743 --> 00:54:07,744
[friend 1] Sigh.

861
00:54:08,745 --> 00:54:10,497
[door lock beeping]

862
00:54:10,580 --> 00:54:11,915
[click - door]

863
00:54:11,998 --> 00:54:13,541
[Ha-min] Ha...

864
00:54:13,625 --> 00:54:14,751
[thud - door]

865
00:54:20,006 --> 00:54:21,299
Ha...

866
00:54:41,528 --> 00:54:43,446
[clattering]

867
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:44,572
Ah...

868
00:55:18,898 --> 00:55:20,066
Ah!

869
00:55:23,028 --> 00:55:24,070
Ugh...

870
00:55:27,032 --> 00:55:28,158
[click - mouse]

871
00:55:34,706 --> 00:55:35,665
Are you married?

872
00:55:37,042 --> 00:55:39,044
- Not yet.
- What about family?

873
00:55:39,669 --> 00:55:40,670
My mom and me.

874
00:55:40,754 --> 00:55:41,755
Where is your mother?

875
00:55:42,922 --> 00:55:44,507
- Back in my hometown.
- Where's your hometown?

876
00:55:44,591 --> 00:55:45,592
Busan.

877
00:55:45,675 --> 00:55:46,926
I'm from Busan too.

878
00:55:47,010 --> 00:55:48,678
- Busan High.
- I went to Gyeongnam High.

879
00:55:54,517 --> 00:55:55,769
Good.

880
00:55:56,436 --> 00:55:57,270
Pardon?

881
00:55:57,353 --> 00:55:58,438
Then what about your father?

882
00:55:59,105 --> 00:56:01,274
Ah, he passed away from stomach cancer.

883
00:56:01,357 --> 00:56:03,443
- When?
- The day I was born.

884
00:56:04,527 --> 00:56:05,528
Good.

885
00:56:05,612 --> 00:56:06,946
Good?

886
00:56:07,030 --> 00:56:09,449
When was your last health checkup?

887
00:56:09,532 --> 00:56:11,451
- I haven't had one yet...
- Why not?

888
00:56:11,534 --> 00:56:12,744
I was too busy making a living.

889
00:56:12,827 --> 00:56:13,912
What do you do?

890
00:56:13,995 --> 00:56:15,205
I sell alcohol.

891
00:56:15,288 --> 00:56:17,290
Ah, alcohol.

892
00:56:18,708 --> 00:56:20,251
I work for a liquor company.

893
00:56:23,963 --> 00:56:25,090
Good.

894
00:56:25,799 --> 00:56:27,926
No, what exactly keeps being good?

895
00:56:29,344 --> 00:56:30,220
It's stomach cancer.

896
00:56:30,303 --> 00:56:32,347
[calm music]

897
00:56:34,182 --> 00:56:36,351
Three months at most.

898
00:56:36,434 --> 00:56:39,395
The younger you are,
the faster it progresses.

899
00:56:41,815 --> 00:56:43,483
[doctor] We can try surgery,

900
00:56:44,317 --> 00:56:46,152
but it's late-stage 3,

901
00:56:47,570 --> 00:56:49,155
and you have a family history,
so it's hard to guarantee anything.

902
00:56:52,325 --> 00:56:54,452
[Ha-min/flashback] If Mom hadn't
kept telling him to eat,

903
00:56:54,536 --> 00:56:56,788
he wouldn't have been hit by a car!

904
00:56:56,871 --> 00:56:58,623
[Eun-sil] Are you afraid you'll die

905
00:56:58,706 --> 00:56:59,916
if you eat the food Mom makes?

906
00:56:59,999 --> 00:57:01,251
[Ha-min] I really can't stand
looking at you.

907
00:57:01,334 --> 00:57:03,419
Do you know what it's like
to live your whole life anxious

908
00:57:03,503 --> 00:57:04,963
because of that damn number?

909
00:57:07,507 --> 00:57:10,718
[Ha-min/narration] Was this something
that could only end if I died?

910
00:57:11,886 --> 00:57:13,429
If I die,

911
00:57:13,513 --> 00:57:15,849
Mom's number will never go down again.

912
00:57:20,645 --> 00:57:21,604
[phone beeps]

913
00:57:22,355 --> 00:57:23,731
[Ryeo-eun] Oppa.

914
00:57:23,815 --> 00:57:25,483
Nothing happened to you, right?

915
00:57:26,526 --> 00:57:28,486
I'm so worried because
I can't reach you.

916
00:57:29,529 --> 00:57:31,197
Let's meet just one last time.

917
00:57:34,784 --> 00:57:36,786
[soft music playing]

918
00:58:00,518 --> 00:58:03,438
I thought about it carefully.

919
00:58:06,608 --> 00:58:07,984
Later, when we have a baby...

920
00:58:10,737 --> 00:58:12,864
Then again,
you don't believe what I say, do you?

921
00:58:14,866 --> 00:58:15,825
Anyway,

922
00:58:17,827 --> 00:58:20,330
you don't even know
what illnesses your birth parents had.

923
00:58:21,748 --> 00:58:23,166
What if our child inherits
your family history?

924
00:58:24,709 --> 00:58:27,587
I'm sick of marriage
and having kids now.

925
00:58:29,797 --> 00:58:30,882
Let's just stop seeing each other.

926
00:58:39,265 --> 00:58:42,018
You know exactly how I grew up.
Do you really have to say it like that?

927
00:58:42,101 --> 00:58:44,020
Stop thinking

928
00:58:44,771 --> 00:58:45,772
you're the most pitiful person
in the world.

929
00:58:47,941 --> 00:58:49,234
I'm sick of it.

930
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:55,615
Fine, let's break up.

931
00:58:57,951 --> 00:59:00,203
You don't deserve to have a family.

932
00:59:00,286 --> 00:59:02,413
You're really selfish.
You only care about yourself.

933
00:59:02,497 --> 00:59:03,373
That's right.

934
00:59:04,958 --> 00:59:05,959
I only care about myself.

935
00:59:08,294 --> 00:59:09,754
I don't care about family at all.

936
00:59:13,341 --> 00:59:14,551
You too.

937
00:59:14,634 --> 00:59:17,303
Meet a man who can handle
your inferiority complex well,

938
00:59:17,387 --> 00:59:18,930
and live happily.

939
00:59:35,405 --> 00:59:36,573
[door clicks]

940
00:59:40,910 --> 00:59:45,582
[announcement] The 10:15 KTX train
bound for Busan will arrive shortly.

941
00:59:45,665 --> 00:59:49,419
Passengers, please wait
behind the safety line...

942
00:59:49,502 --> 00:59:51,504
[soft music]

943
01:00:04,726 --> 01:00:06,102
[child crying]

944
01:00:07,562 --> 01:00:09,939
- [woman 1] Oh...
- [child 1] Mom!

945
01:00:10,023 --> 01:00:11,482
[woman 2/tearfully] Mom.

946
01:00:11,566 --> 01:00:12,817
I failed.

947
01:00:12,900 --> 01:00:14,444
Mom, I want to eat
the tteokbokki you make.

948
01:00:14,527 --> 01:00:16,112
- [woman 3] Should I make tteokbokki?
- [student] Yeah.

949
01:00:16,195 --> 01:00:17,697
[child 2] Mom.

950
01:00:18,281 --> 01:00:20,199
[Ha-min/narration]
We humans are strange.

951
01:00:21,409 --> 01:00:22,619
[child 2/crying] Mom!

952
01:00:22,702 --> 01:00:23,786
[Ha-min/narration] When we're in danger,

953
01:00:23,870 --> 01:00:26,956
before saying,
"Please save me" or "Please help me,"

954
01:00:27,040 --> 01:00:28,499
we call for Mom first.

955
01:00:29,584 --> 01:00:30,460
[child 2/crying] Mom!

956
01:00:30,543 --> 01:00:32,045
The number or whatever else...

957
01:00:33,212 --> 01:00:34,255
I don't care anymore.

958
01:00:37,550 --> 01:00:39,552
[calm music]

959
01:00:47,060 --> 01:00:48,269
[birds chirping]

960
01:00:56,736 --> 01:00:58,196
[children chattering in the distance]

961
01:01:24,806 --> 01:01:25,932
My son.

962
01:01:28,101 --> 01:01:31,104
Both my sons are dead.

963
01:01:31,896 --> 01:01:33,690
What are you talking about?
I'm alive right here.

964
01:01:33,773 --> 01:01:35,441
No, no.

965
01:01:36,275 --> 01:01:38,903
The first one got hit by a car,

966
01:01:38,986 --> 01:01:41,406
and the second one went into the water.

967
01:01:41,489 --> 01:01:44,534
A woman with no luck with children
has no luck with her husband either.

968
01:01:44,617 --> 01:01:45,618
I have neither.

969
01:01:45,702 --> 01:01:48,746
Huh? When did I ever go into the water?

970
01:01:49,706 --> 01:01:51,082
I don't even go to pools,
let alone the sea.

971
01:01:51,874 --> 01:01:52,834
Mom, do you have dementia?

972
01:01:53,459 --> 01:01:54,794
But who are you really?

973
01:01:55,962 --> 01:01:59,048
Goodness, are you my son's friend?

974
01:01:59,966 --> 01:02:03,970
Or are you the new public-service worker
from the neighborhood office?

975
01:02:04,637 --> 01:02:07,557
Stop joking around.
It's me, Ha-min.

976
01:02:07,640 --> 01:02:10,059
I'm telling you, I really don't know you.

977
01:02:10,143 --> 01:02:11,978
Do you look down on me
because I'm a woman living alone?

978
01:02:12,979 --> 01:02:14,105
Why are you being so scary?

979
01:02:15,314 --> 01:02:16,274
Ah...

980
01:02:17,483 --> 01:02:18,735
D-Dementia?

981
01:02:19,944 --> 01:02:20,820
Ah...

982
01:02:22,655 --> 01:02:23,906
{\an8}What's 5 times 8?

983
01:02:29,370 --> 01:02:31,080
Ah, what the hell!

984
01:02:31,164 --> 01:02:32,415
Hey, Mom is a good actress, right?

985
01:02:32,498 --> 01:02:33,458
Are you crazy?

986
01:02:33,541 --> 01:02:35,835
- How can you ask your mom if she's crazy?
- [Ha-min] Ah...

987
01:02:35,918 --> 01:02:37,086
You scared me!

988
01:02:37,170 --> 01:02:39,338
Why did you come here,
after saying you couldn't stand to look at me?

989
01:02:39,964 --> 01:02:41,966
Damn it, I came to eat your food.

990
01:02:42,675 --> 01:02:43,843
What food is there?

991
01:02:43,926 --> 01:02:45,136
There isn't any food?

992
01:02:45,219 --> 01:02:47,638
I live alone.
How could I cook rice every day?

993
01:02:47,722 --> 01:02:49,182
My arms and legs ache like crazy.

994
01:02:50,600 --> 01:02:52,351
[sighs] What do you want to eat?

995
01:02:53,519 --> 01:02:54,437
Beef soup.

996
01:02:59,442 --> 01:03:00,860
[Eun-sil] But why are you so skinny?

997
01:03:06,699 --> 01:03:08,034
[Eun-sil] Haha, hello.

998
01:03:08,785 --> 01:03:10,328
Ah, hello.

999
01:03:11,120 --> 01:03:13,623
- Boss!
- [owner] Oh, welcome.

1000
01:03:13,706 --> 01:03:15,792
Beef for soup.
Give me one geun.

1001
01:03:15,875 --> 01:03:17,460
No, give me one and a half geun.

1002
01:03:17,543 --> 01:03:19,128
Oh, what's this?

1003
01:03:19,212 --> 01:03:20,171
Starting a new household?

1004
01:03:20,254 --> 01:03:22,256
My son came home.

1005
01:03:23,216 --> 01:03:24,300
- [owner] Must be nice.
- Don't trim off the fat.

1006
01:03:24,383 --> 01:03:25,259
Just give it to me as is.

1007
01:03:25,343 --> 01:03:27,094
My boy likes it
when the oil floats on top.

1008
01:03:27,178 --> 01:03:28,304
[owner] Got it.

1009
01:03:32,225 --> 01:03:34,143
[Eun-sil] What, are there no side dishes?

1010
01:03:34,227 --> 01:03:35,645
Huh? No, that's not it.

1011
01:03:35,728 --> 01:03:37,063
What, you have no appetite?

1012
01:03:37,146 --> 01:03:39,148
- No.
- What, you have no manners?

1013
01:03:39,232 --> 01:03:41,526
Wow, Mom, you've still got it.

1014
01:03:41,609 --> 01:03:43,736
Then do you wish your mom was dead?

1015
01:03:43,820 --> 01:03:45,071
Stop talking back and eat.

1016
01:03:46,906 --> 01:03:47,824
[Ha-min] Ha...

1017
01:03:47,907 --> 01:03:48,825
Huh?

1018
01:03:49,992 --> 01:03:51,077
Why is your soup like that, Mom?

1019
01:03:51,160 --> 01:03:53,454
I told you, I can't eat meat.

1020
01:03:53,538 --> 01:03:54,747
Did you forget already?

1021
01:03:54,831 --> 01:03:56,833
Oh, right. Sorry.

1022
01:03:56,916 --> 01:03:59,001
It's only meat I can't eat.
I can eat everything else.

1023
01:04:00,586 --> 01:04:01,754
Stop putting on a show and eat.

1024
01:04:01,838 --> 01:04:04,131
- Thank you for the meal.
- [Eun-sil] Mm.

1025
01:04:08,261 --> 01:04:09,345
Mm~

1026
01:04:10,638 --> 01:04:11,889
Is it good?

1027
01:04:13,266 --> 01:04:14,767
[Eun-sil laughing]

1028
01:04:15,935 --> 01:04:17,979
[calm music]

1029
01:04:19,939 --> 01:04:21,274
[Eun-sil] Goodness.

1030
01:04:24,986 --> 01:04:26,696
[mysterious sound effect]

1031
01:04:34,912 --> 01:04:36,622
Ha, this is seriously so good.

1032
01:04:36,706 --> 01:04:37,915
[Eun-sil laughing]

1033
01:04:46,257 --> 01:04:47,967
[Eun-sil] Don't they have Daiso in Seoul?

1034
01:04:48,050 --> 01:04:49,051
[Ha-min] There are lots.

1035
01:04:50,303 --> 01:04:51,846
Then buy a nail clipper for 1,000 won.

1036
01:04:51,929 --> 01:04:54,765
You're in sales,
but look at your nails. Tsk.

1037
01:04:54,849 --> 01:04:55,892
I told you before.

1038
01:04:57,476 --> 01:04:58,769
Only Mom cuts my nails.

1039
01:04:58,853 --> 01:04:59,812
[Eun-sil chuckles softly]

1040
01:05:02,481 --> 01:05:03,941
- But, Mom...
- [Eun-sil] Mm?

1041
01:05:04,734 --> 01:05:07,695
How long did Dad live
after the surgery?

1042
01:05:10,948 --> 01:05:14,076
[Eun-sil] About three days
in the ICU.

1043
01:05:14,160 --> 01:05:15,828
He just lay there and passed away.

1044
01:05:16,871 --> 01:05:18,497
Your dad was impatient, wasn't he?

1045
01:05:20,082 --> 01:05:21,667
He could've opened his eyes
even for a moment

1046
01:05:25,671 --> 01:05:27,006
so he could see you before he went.

1047
01:05:34,055 --> 01:05:35,139
- Mom.
- [Eun-sil] Yeah?

1048
01:05:36,307 --> 01:05:38,184
Should I stay a little longer?

1049
01:05:40,186 --> 01:05:42,813
Did you get fired or something?

1050
01:05:42,897 --> 01:05:44,440
Come on, what are you talking about?

1051
01:05:45,524 --> 01:05:47,360
Other companies are fighting
to take me.

1052
01:05:47,443 --> 01:05:49,153
Then why?

1053
01:05:50,029 --> 01:05:51,322
Just because.

1054
01:05:51,405 --> 01:05:54,200
I want to eat Mom's food
to my heart's content before I go.

1055
01:05:54,825 --> 01:05:57,328
Bullshit.
You said bought food tastes better.

1056
01:05:57,411 --> 01:05:59,497
Come on, that's only for a day or two.

1057
01:06:02,875 --> 01:06:03,960
How long will you stay?

1058
01:06:11,759 --> 01:06:12,760
[Ha-min] Ha...

1059
01:06:13,761 --> 01:06:15,429
It's only about a month.

1060
01:06:19,100 --> 01:06:19,976
Ah.

1061
01:06:21,477 --> 01:06:22,687
Ah...

1062
01:06:25,231 --> 01:06:26,190
Ah...

1063
01:06:27,566 --> 01:06:29,610
[calm music]

1064
01:06:51,549 --> 01:06:53,134
[Eun-sil] What do you want
for dinner?

1065
01:06:58,139 --> 01:07:00,057
[employee 1] Did you have
a good trip home?

1066
01:07:00,141 --> 01:07:01,017
[team leader] Oh, well...

1067
01:07:01,600 --> 01:07:03,394
Right, you all said
you're from Busan, didn't you?

1068
01:07:03,978 --> 01:07:04,895
[all] Yes.

1069
01:07:07,148 --> 01:07:10,609
At most, I see my parents twice a year,
on Lunar New Year and Chuseok.

1070
01:07:11,235 --> 01:07:13,320
And since I'm from Jeju,

1071
01:07:13,404 --> 01:07:16,198
if a typhoon comes,
like last Chuseok, I just skip that too.

1072
01:07:16,949 --> 01:07:20,202
Even if Mom and Dad
have 20 years left,

1073
01:07:21,120 --> 01:07:24,123
that means I'll only see them
exactly 40 more times.

1074
01:07:24,206 --> 01:07:26,125
- [employee 1] Huh?
- Forty times.

1075
01:07:27,960 --> 01:07:29,378
That's chilling, huh?

1076
01:07:29,462 --> 01:07:31,130
When you say it's suddenly
only 40 times...

1077
01:07:32,131 --> 01:07:33,049
You're right.

1078
01:07:35,634 --> 01:07:38,512
Your wife may wait for you at home,
but your parents won't wait.

1079
01:07:40,139 --> 01:07:41,932
[employee 2] Ugh! It's cold, damn it.

1080
01:07:42,558 --> 01:07:44,018
- [employee 3] Hello, sir.
- [employee 2] Yeah.

1081
01:07:44,894 --> 01:07:46,228
No, but seriously,

1082
01:07:46,312 --> 01:07:47,855
what's so fun with this team

1083
01:07:47,938 --> 01:07:50,566
that whenever they get time,
they gather and whisper among themselves?

1084
01:07:50,649 --> 01:07:52,109
What's so fun, huh?

1085
01:07:54,612 --> 01:07:55,446
Hyungnim.

1086
01:07:56,614 --> 01:07:57,823
I heard Jung Ha-min quit.

1087
01:07:58,783 --> 01:07:59,742
Pardon?

1088
01:07:59,825 --> 01:08:01,660
[employee 2] Ha-min, that guy...

1089
01:08:01,744 --> 01:08:04,914
He even brought in that somaek lady,
so your position was looking shaky.

1090
01:08:04,997 --> 01:08:05,831
This worked out well.

1091
01:08:05,915 --> 01:08:06,957
- Hyungnim, aren't you throwing a party?
- [team leader] Hey.

1092
01:08:07,041 --> 01:08:08,918
- Smoke your cigarette.
- [employee 2] Oh, right...

1093
01:08:09,001 --> 01:08:10,419
[team leader] If you came out to smoke,
then smoke.

1094
01:08:10,503 --> 01:08:12,797
Right, Executive Kim
was looking for you earlier.

1095
01:08:12,880 --> 01:08:13,756
- Huh?
- [team leader] Yeah, hurry up and go.

1096
01:08:13,839 --> 01:08:15,633
[employee 2] Why?
What did Executive Kim say this time?

1097
01:08:15,716 --> 01:08:18,469
Just hurry up and go.
You'll find out when you get there.

1098
01:08:18,552 --> 01:08:20,179
[employee 2] Why again? Ah!

1099
01:08:20,763 --> 01:08:21,639
[employee 1] What do you mean, he quit?

1100
01:08:23,265 --> 01:08:25,309
Ah, that bastard, seriously.

1101
01:08:28,229 --> 01:08:30,356
He told me not to tell you guys.

1102
01:08:30,439 --> 01:08:32,441
[calm music]

1103
01:08:40,199 --> 01:08:41,826
[phone vibrating]

1104
01:08:52,503 --> 01:08:55,214
[Eun-sil] Oh, Ryeo-eun,
did you call?

1105
01:08:57,466 --> 01:08:59,051
- Mom.
- [Eun-sil] Yes?

1106
01:09:01,971 --> 01:09:03,180
Oppa...

1107
01:09:18,821 --> 01:09:20,823
[music intensifies]

1108
01:10:11,582 --> 01:10:14,001
But before dying,
this is all you wanted to eat?

1109
01:10:14,084 --> 01:10:15,085
[Ha-min] Ha!

1110
01:10:15,169 --> 01:10:17,254
Try it first.
Eat it, then say that.

1111
01:10:18,380 --> 01:10:19,215
Here.

1112
01:10:24,970 --> 01:10:25,888
I don't get it.

1113
01:10:25,971 --> 01:10:27,306
Hey!

1114
01:10:27,389 --> 01:10:29,141
Geoin Tongdak is my life, okay?

1115
01:10:29,225 --> 01:10:32,186
When I went up to Seoul,
this was what I missed the most.

1116
01:10:33,103 --> 01:10:36,357
Junko, Yoogane, Okkudak, Mubwatna—
they all went up to Seoul,

1117
01:10:37,149 --> 01:10:38,442
but this place is still the same.

1118
01:10:41,278 --> 01:10:43,572
Actually, I came to say goodbye.

1119
01:10:45,032 --> 01:10:46,742
Goodbye, Geoin Tongdak.

1120
01:10:46,825 --> 01:10:47,952
See you in my next life.

1121
01:10:49,787 --> 01:10:50,621
Come here.

1122
01:10:53,165 --> 01:10:54,500
[Ha-min chuckles softly]

1123
01:10:55,376 --> 01:10:57,211
Wow, this is seriously delicious.

1124
01:11:01,173 --> 01:11:03,676
What else was it
that I wanted to eat again?

1125
01:11:04,593 --> 01:11:07,596
They say when you get stomach cancer,
all you think about is food. I guess it's true.

1126
01:11:07,680 --> 01:11:09,932
Ahp, you searched it up again.

1127
01:11:10,516 --> 01:11:13,852
Anemic, skinny as a rail,
eyes sunken, and skin rough like a sweet potato.

1128
01:11:14,812 --> 01:11:15,646
What else?

1129
01:11:15,729 --> 01:11:17,064
- Hair loss.
- Ugh!

1130
01:11:17,856 --> 01:11:20,484
Hair loss? No, not hair loss.
That's my last shred of pride.

1131
01:11:20,567 --> 01:11:22,444
Well, look who thinks he's Mr. Hairpiece.

1132
01:11:25,197 --> 01:11:27,116
- This is your punishment, Oppa.
- Ahp!

1133
01:11:27,199 --> 01:11:29,451
Damn it, that "ahp, ahp, ahp"!

1134
01:11:29,535 --> 01:11:31,412
What the hell is "ahp" anyway?

1135
01:11:33,455 --> 01:11:34,707
You're dying, but your mouth is still alive.

1136
01:11:38,836 --> 01:11:41,463
Anyway, I'm not a doctor or anything,
so I can't save you.

1137
01:11:42,214 --> 01:11:43,090
Goodbye.

1138
01:11:52,433 --> 01:11:55,019
But still, watching you eat
makes me feel good.

1139
01:12:07,948 --> 01:12:09,116
Someone who's going to leave anyway...

1140
01:12:10,075 --> 01:12:11,243
I'll try holding on to him one last time.

1141
01:12:13,746 --> 01:12:15,664
And I'll let him go properly, without regrets.

1142
01:12:20,544 --> 01:12:21,587
[door clicks]

1143
01:12:23,047 --> 01:12:24,006
[door shuts]

1144
01:12:26,967 --> 01:12:29,219
[Ha-min] What are you doing?
Let's eat.

1145
01:12:35,642 --> 01:12:36,769
What did you do with all of it?

1146
01:12:38,187 --> 01:12:39,146
[fridge door shuts]

1147
01:12:39,229 --> 01:12:41,857
I threw it all away.

1148
01:12:42,566 --> 01:12:43,400
What?

1149
01:12:48,113 --> 01:12:49,031
Why?

1150
01:12:50,574 --> 01:12:51,658
What's the point of eating?

1151
01:12:53,369 --> 01:12:54,620
You're going to throw it all up anyway.

1152
01:13:03,212 --> 01:13:04,838
How long were you planning
to fool your mom?

1153
01:13:07,216 --> 01:13:09,259
What do you mean, fool you?

1154
01:13:10,803 --> 01:13:12,638
You said I lost weight
as soon as you saw me.

1155
01:13:23,357 --> 01:13:24,400
[Eun-sil] Ha...

1156
01:13:28,278 --> 01:13:30,572
Get the surgery.

1157
01:13:34,660 --> 01:13:37,413
Dad had surgery too,
and you said he never woke up.

1158
01:13:37,496 --> 01:13:40,249
I'd rather spend a few more days with you.

1159
01:13:40,332 --> 01:13:42,126
It's been so long since I ate your food.
It tastes good.

1160
01:13:43,710 --> 01:13:45,254
If I go to the afterlife,
I won't be able to eat your cooking.

1161
01:13:46,130 --> 01:13:47,005
You little...

1162
01:13:48,424 --> 01:13:50,342
Is that something a child says to his parent?

1163
01:13:53,011 --> 01:13:55,264
Like you always say,
just think of it as fate.

1164
01:13:56,056 --> 01:13:57,307
At this point, it really is fate.

1165
01:14:06,066 --> 01:14:08,152
[heavy music]

1166
01:14:14,032 --> 01:14:16,160
[sniffling]

1167
01:14:20,122 --> 01:14:22,332
{\an8}I'll beg you like this.

1168
01:14:24,668 --> 01:14:25,711
{\an8}With Mom...

1169
01:14:27,296 --> 01:14:28,297
{\an8}let's go to the hospital.

1170
01:14:30,674 --> 01:14:33,844
Is now the same as
when your father died?

1171
01:14:35,053 --> 01:14:37,055
That was over 30 years ago.

1172
01:14:40,225 --> 01:14:42,436
{\an8}Do you know what it's like

1173
01:14:44,062 --> 01:14:45,439
{\an8}to send your child off before you?

1174
01:14:51,528 --> 01:14:54,406
{\an8}After sending your brother off like that,

1175
01:14:57,409 --> 01:14:58,410
{\an8}not once...

1176
01:15:00,204 --> 01:15:02,915
{\an8}not once did I put toner or lotion
on my face.

1177
01:15:08,212 --> 01:15:10,797
{\an8}I haven't lived a single day properly.

1178
01:15:12,257 --> 01:15:13,258
Because you...

1179
01:15:15,093 --> 01:15:16,929
Because you came back to me,

1180
01:15:17,888 --> 01:15:20,432
I thought I should finally live properly too.

1181
01:15:26,730 --> 01:15:28,315
Are you going to do this to me too?

1182
01:15:34,613 --> 01:15:36,949
My life is mine,
so why are you telling me what to do?

1183
01:15:38,909 --> 01:15:41,662
Because I'm your mom. Your mom.

1184
01:15:45,749 --> 01:15:47,543
Forget it. I'll take care of it myself.

1185
01:15:52,422 --> 01:15:53,549
[door clicks]

1186
01:15:53,632 --> 01:15:54,758
Ugh...

1187
01:15:55,801 --> 01:15:57,010
- Ugh...
- [door shuts]

1188
01:15:57,970 --> 01:15:59,972
[pained groaning]

1189
01:16:45,350 --> 01:16:46,977
Ha...

1190
01:16:47,060 --> 01:16:48,061
[sniffling]

1191
01:16:53,525 --> 01:16:54,651
[Ha-min retching]

1192
01:16:55,444 --> 01:16:56,612
[Ha-min coughing]

1193
01:16:59,031 --> 01:17:00,407
[Ha-min breathing heavily]

1194
01:17:43,200 --> 01:17:45,243
[heavy music]

1195
01:17:54,169 --> 01:17:55,128
[YouTuber/video]
You have soaked garlic?

1196
01:17:55,212 --> 01:17:56,672
[woman/video] Aren't we supposed
to add soaked garlic?

1197
01:17:56,755 --> 01:17:58,674
- No, soaked seaweed.
- Seaweed. Add that in.

1198
01:17:58,757 --> 01:18:00,258
[woman/video]
We're supposed to add soaked seaweed, right?

1199
01:18:06,973 --> 01:18:09,226
[soft music playing]

1200
01:18:09,309 --> 01:18:10,852
[Ryeo-eun] How is Oppa doing?

1201
01:18:25,075 --> 01:18:27,285
What is he planning to do,
acting like that?

1202
01:18:27,369 --> 01:18:29,705
Ugh, it's making my blood boil.

1203
01:18:30,622 --> 01:18:31,915
Sigh.

1204
01:18:34,710 --> 01:18:37,003
Even if you're going to break up,

1205
01:18:37,087 --> 01:18:39,381
try persuading him first.

1206
01:18:40,424 --> 01:18:42,217
Tell him to get the surgery right away.

1207
01:18:44,720 --> 01:18:47,973
Men may not listen to their mothers,

1208
01:18:48,974 --> 01:18:50,976
but they listen to women, don't they?

1209
01:18:55,689 --> 01:18:56,565
Mom.

1210
01:18:57,691 --> 01:18:59,443
You love Ha-min Oppa, right?

1211
01:18:59,526 --> 01:19:02,821
Of course I love him.
He's my child.

1212
01:19:04,156 --> 01:19:05,157
What is love?

1213
01:19:05,907 --> 01:19:08,618
It's believing someone,
even if they say something impossible.

1214
01:19:11,455 --> 01:19:13,248
We don't know when Oppa will leave us,

1215
01:19:14,374 --> 01:19:15,625
so let's try believing him.

1216
01:19:17,669 --> 01:19:18,837
Believing what?

1217
01:19:20,839 --> 01:19:22,632
The thing that keeps tormenting him...

1218
01:19:23,675 --> 01:19:24,718
that number.

1219
01:19:26,636 --> 01:19:28,263
[foghorn in the distance]

1220
01:19:29,514 --> 01:19:31,349
[Ryeo-eun] Add the fish sauce.

1221
01:19:32,851 --> 01:19:34,102
Here.

1222
01:19:34,186 --> 01:19:35,604
[Ha-min] Oh, you know how to eat this.

1223
01:19:40,776 --> 01:19:42,110
[Ryeo-eun] Mm!

1224
01:19:50,368 --> 01:19:51,620
Wow!

1225
01:19:51,703 --> 01:19:54,539
Wow, you eat pork rice soup well.
Doesn't it smell gamey?

1226
01:19:54,623 --> 01:19:57,167
Isn't it basically the same
as soondae soup?

1227
01:19:57,250 --> 01:19:58,585
[Ha-min] Hey.

1228
01:19:58,668 --> 01:20:00,378
Say that in Busan,
and you'll get slapped.

1229
01:20:01,129 --> 01:20:03,965
The pig's passion
as it dives into the broth is different.

1230
01:20:04,049 --> 01:20:05,425
Wow, look who thinks he's a Korean cuisine master.

1231
01:20:05,509 --> 01:20:06,885
Hey, damn it.

1232
01:20:10,388 --> 01:20:12,808
Why did you come back down here?

1233
01:20:12,891 --> 01:20:13,892
I told you I'd hold on to you.

1234
01:20:17,604 --> 01:20:18,647
Be honest.

1235
01:20:20,065 --> 01:20:21,191
You still love me, right?

1236
01:20:21,274 --> 01:20:22,901
- Yeah.
- Huh?

1237
01:20:23,485 --> 01:20:26,404
Hey, how can you just say "yeah"?
How am I supposed to die now?

1238
01:20:27,906 --> 01:20:29,908
So what are you going to do from now on?

1239
01:20:29,991 --> 01:20:31,368
Mm...

1240
01:20:34,246 --> 01:20:35,580
I'll die leaving one behind.

1241
01:20:36,373 --> 01:20:38,458
Are you a KakaoTalk message?
You're going to die leaving a "1"?

1242
01:20:43,797 --> 01:20:45,090
To be honest,

1243
01:20:45,799 --> 01:20:48,510
I don't really know
what you're feeling toward your mom right now.

1244
01:20:48,593 --> 01:20:49,594
I never learned that.

1245
01:20:56,434 --> 01:20:58,270
Anyway, stop messing around
and get the surgery soon.

1246
01:20:59,271 --> 01:21:02,107
And I thought about it carefully.

1247
01:21:02,941 --> 01:21:03,859
About what?

1248
01:21:04,526 --> 01:21:07,070
A way to save you
from the curse of the number.

1249
01:21:08,196 --> 01:21:09,364
You believe me now?

1250
01:21:09,447 --> 01:21:11,032
Yeah.

1251
01:21:11,116 --> 01:21:14,619
In Latin, "Animum fortuna sequitur."

1252
01:21:14,703 --> 01:21:16,788
Do you know the saying,
"Fortune follows courage"?

1253
01:21:17,372 --> 01:21:19,124
Wow, look who thinks she's Harry Potter.

1254
01:21:19,207 --> 01:21:20,458
Forget it. Just die, then.

1255
01:21:20,542 --> 01:21:21,835
Sorry. What is it?

1256
01:21:21,918 --> 01:21:23,086
Forget it.

1257
01:21:23,169 --> 01:21:26,423
Come on, I'm about to die.
Let me off just this once.

1258
01:21:28,133 --> 01:21:30,135
[calm music]

1259
01:21:37,601 --> 01:21:38,977
Actually, Ryeo-eun...

1260
01:21:45,358 --> 01:21:46,818
I don't want to die like this.

1261
01:21:56,328 --> 01:21:57,913
[tearful breathing]

1262
01:22:03,543 --> 01:22:05,253
[Ha-min sobbing]

1263
01:22:16,598 --> 01:22:17,557
I'm sorry.

1264
01:22:19,142 --> 01:22:20,018
I'm sorry.

1265
01:22:43,083 --> 01:22:44,376
[rustling plastic]

1266
01:23:03,770 --> 01:23:04,854
At least tell me.

1267
01:23:06,231 --> 01:23:07,315
Sigh.

1268
01:23:11,987 --> 01:23:13,071
Ugh.

1269
01:23:15,240 --> 01:23:16,491
Tch...

1270
01:23:23,248 --> 01:23:26,835
Slice the radish really thin,
like you're sharpening pencils,

1271
01:23:26,918 --> 01:23:28,003
then put the beef in the oil.

1272
01:23:28,086 --> 01:23:29,671
Oh, right. You have to buy brisket.

1273
01:23:29,754 --> 01:23:31,089
Don't go to the supermarket
just because you're lazy

1274
01:23:31,172 --> 01:23:32,674
- [rhythmic music]
- and grab some prepacked meat.

1275
01:23:32,757 --> 01:23:34,259
Go to the butcher shop
and ask for one geun

1276
01:23:34,342 --> 01:23:35,427
with the fat still attached.

1277
01:23:35,510 --> 01:23:36,386
Think about it.

1278
01:23:36,469 --> 01:23:38,430
How could the soup taste good
if it's only dry lean meat?

1279
01:23:38,513 --> 01:23:41,182
There has to be fat,
and oil has to float on top.

1280
01:23:41,266 --> 01:23:42,350
That's the key point.

1281
01:23:42,434 --> 01:23:44,102
Put the beef into the oil,
then add minced garlic.

1282
01:23:44,185 --> 01:23:45,520
You know Joseon soy sauce?
Add one spoonful of that.

1283
01:23:45,603 --> 01:23:47,355
Coarse red pepper powder is better.

1284
01:23:47,439 --> 01:23:49,107
- Stir-fry it until it almost burns in the pot.
- [sizzling sound effect]

1285
01:23:49,190 --> 01:23:51,026
Then add the radish and water.

1286
01:23:51,109 --> 01:23:52,736
If you add the green onions too early,
they'll all turn to mush.

1287
01:23:52,819 --> 01:23:54,696
And don't chop the green onions
all tiny and fussy.

1288
01:23:54,779 --> 01:23:57,198
Just cut them casually. Chop, chop.

1289
01:23:57,949 --> 01:23:58,992
Do you understand?

1290
01:23:59,534 --> 01:24:00,493
[rolling sound effect]

1291
01:24:02,912 --> 01:24:04,247
Mom, are you Outsider or something?

1292
01:24:04,330 --> 01:24:05,874
Speak a little slower!

1293
01:24:06,541 --> 01:24:09,169
Oh my, mother-in-law.

1294
01:24:09,961 --> 01:24:11,296
Listen carefully.

1295
01:24:12,172 --> 01:24:13,548
[clearly] Radish.

1296
01:24:13,631 --> 01:24:16,760
Slice it like you're sharpening a pencil.

1297
01:24:17,802 --> 01:24:19,387
- [Eun-sil] You can tap it like this too.
- [Ha-min] Yeah, oh.

1298
01:24:19,471 --> 01:24:22,057
[Eun-sil] Like this, like this.
Like this. Look.

1299
01:24:22,140 --> 01:24:22,974
[Ha-min] Whew.

1300
01:24:33,068 --> 01:24:34,110
[Ha-min] Yeah.

1301
01:24:41,284 --> 01:24:42,452
Mm...

1302
01:25:09,062 --> 01:25:11,356
[calm music]

1303
01:25:12,649 --> 01:25:14,109
[mysterious sound effect]

1304
01:25:26,329 --> 01:25:27,622
Mom.

1305
01:25:27,705 --> 01:25:28,581
Yeah?

1306
01:25:29,374 --> 01:25:30,708
I'm going to have the surgery.

1307
01:25:34,629 --> 01:25:36,047
But...

1308
01:25:36,131 --> 01:25:38,299
if I don't wake up,
don't cremate me, no matter what.

1309
01:25:39,551 --> 01:25:41,386
Bury me somewhere sunny
with an ocean view.

1310
01:25:45,890 --> 01:25:47,725
Why did you suddenly change your mind?

1311
01:25:50,061 --> 01:25:50,937
Just because.

1312
01:25:52,772 --> 01:25:54,065
I feel so sorry for you.

1313
01:25:56,568 --> 01:25:57,610
Why do you feel sorry for me?

1314
01:25:59,112 --> 01:26:00,572
When I think about it,

1315
01:26:01,906 --> 01:26:04,868
Grandpa didn't even let you go to school,
so you couldn't study.

1316
01:26:06,161 --> 01:26:08,580
And you spent your whole life
taking care of me and Hyung,

1317
01:26:09,372 --> 01:26:11,416
without even knowing
what you wanted to do.

1318
01:26:14,878 --> 01:26:16,838
{\an8}In Seoul, women your age

1319
01:26:17,672 --> 01:26:20,675
{\an8}are professors and National Assembly members.

1320
01:26:21,926 --> 01:26:23,469
{\an8}They're living life to the fullest.

1321
01:26:26,055 --> 01:26:27,515
{\an8}And I felt so sorry for you.

1322
01:26:30,351 --> 01:26:31,853
Well, my goodness.

1323
01:26:31,936 --> 01:26:34,981
They say boys finally mature before they die.
That's exactly you.

1324
01:26:38,985 --> 01:26:40,028
Ms. Eun-sil.

1325
01:26:44,032 --> 01:26:45,617
In your next life,

1326
01:26:45,700 --> 01:26:47,452
be born as my child.

1327
01:26:48,828 --> 01:26:52,123
I'll send you to college
and let you do everything you want.

1328
01:26:54,500 --> 01:26:56,127
That mouth of yours is still alive.

1329
01:26:59,631 --> 01:27:00,506
And...

1330
01:27:03,384 --> 01:27:07,096
at Hyung's funeral,
I heard everything people were saying.

1331
01:27:08,973 --> 01:27:10,642
That you killed your husband,

1332
01:27:11,851 --> 01:27:13,186
then killed your child too,

1333
01:27:14,020 --> 01:27:15,271
and that it was all your fault.

1334
01:27:19,817 --> 01:27:20,652
But...

1335
01:27:23,863 --> 01:27:24,822
Dad...

1336
01:27:26,908 --> 01:27:29,202
me, and Hyung too...

1337
01:27:36,876 --> 01:27:38,086
none of it was your fault.

1338
01:27:40,713 --> 01:27:42,757
[calm music continues]

1339
01:27:53,268 --> 01:27:55,645
{\an8}Thank you, even just for saying that.

1340
01:28:10,910 --> 01:28:12,370
[seagulls crying]

1341
01:28:50,199 --> 01:28:52,243
Oh my, mother-in-law.

1342
01:28:53,202 --> 01:28:56,539
There's nothing scarier in this world
than a mother-in-law.

1343
01:28:56,622 --> 01:28:57,582
Don't be scared.

1344
01:28:58,166 --> 01:28:59,625
Okay. I'll be back.

1345
01:29:01,586 --> 01:29:03,129
[Ha-min's aunt] Go and come back safely.

1346
01:29:10,261 --> 01:29:12,263
[sorrowful music]

1347
01:29:16,726 --> 01:29:17,727
Unnie.

1348
01:29:18,853 --> 01:29:20,355
I'm so scared.

1349
01:29:21,564 --> 01:29:23,691
What if something goes wrong?

1350
01:29:25,860 --> 01:29:29,447
If they take Ha-min too,
from a woman with a twisted fate like me,

1351
01:29:29,530 --> 01:29:32,408
Jesus, Buddha, whatever—
I won't let them get away with it.

1352
01:29:32,492 --> 01:29:33,409
Don't worry.

1353
01:29:33,493 --> 01:29:35,119
[Eun-sil wailing]

1354
01:29:44,587 --> 01:29:45,880
[beeping medical equipment]

1355
01:29:45,963 --> 01:29:47,173
[Ha-min] Oh my, mother-in-law.

1356
01:29:49,342 --> 01:29:50,635
Oh my, mother-in-law.

1357
01:29:52,512 --> 01:29:54,097
[nervous breathing]

1358
01:29:56,641 --> 01:29:58,768
[calm music]

1359
01:30:02,814 --> 01:30:04,107
Oh my, mother-in-law.

1360
01:30:08,194 --> 01:30:09,654
Ha...

1361
01:30:34,011 --> 01:30:35,596
[Ha-jun] The soybean leaves
were really delicious.

1362
01:30:35,680 --> 01:30:36,556
[Eun-sil] Eat a lot.

1363
01:30:37,598 --> 01:30:39,183
They're salty, so eat them one at a time.

1364
01:30:39,267 --> 01:30:40,810
The youngest should do it, shouldn't he?

1365
01:30:45,731 --> 01:30:47,024
[Eun-sil laughing]

1366
01:30:48,192 --> 01:30:49,360
[Ha-min's father laughing]

1367
01:30:52,321 --> 01:30:53,739
[Ha-jun] This tastes like Mom.

1368
01:31:18,181 --> 01:31:20,766
- [beeping medical equipment]
- [hissing respirator]

1369
01:31:26,522 --> 01:31:27,857
[ding-dong]

1370
01:31:31,944 --> 01:31:33,196
[Eun-sil] Ha...

1371
01:31:37,658 --> 01:31:38,576
[Ryeo-eun chuckles softly]

1372
01:32:04,101 --> 01:32:05,102
Thank you.

1373
01:32:37,677 --> 01:32:38,594
Mom.

1374
01:32:38,678 --> 01:32:39,971
[Ha-min's aunt] Goodness.

1375
01:32:40,638 --> 01:32:42,974
That's embarrassing.
How old are you, still saying "Mom"?

1376
01:32:43,641 --> 01:32:45,142
What else should I call my mom
besides Mom?

1377
01:32:45,726 --> 01:32:46,811
Mother.

1378
01:32:46,894 --> 01:32:48,729
Ah, that's so awkward.

1379
01:32:48,813 --> 01:32:49,897
[Ha-min's aunt] What's awkward about it?

1380
01:32:49,981 --> 01:32:52,108
Excuse me, ladies.

1381
01:32:52,191 --> 01:32:54,694
I just knocked on death's door,
so could you please focus?

1382
01:32:55,486 --> 01:32:56,445
Are you okay?

1383
01:32:56,529 --> 01:32:58,864
[Ha-min] Wow, Auntie, you're tough.

1384
01:32:59,532 --> 01:33:02,743
{\an8}Your son just had cancer surgery.
How can you not shed a single tear?

1385
01:33:02,827 --> 01:33:04,328
[Ha-min's aunt] Goodness, why wouldn't she cry?

1386
01:33:04,412 --> 01:33:06,831
Your mom cried and cried so much

1387
01:33:06,914 --> 01:33:09,792
that all the nurses at the hospital
quit because of her.

1388
01:33:09,875 --> 01:33:11,419
[Eun-sil, smacking her] Unnie,
what are you saying?

1389
01:33:11,502 --> 01:33:12,378
Ow, ah...

1390
01:33:12,461 --> 01:33:14,672
Let me talk with my son after so long.
Get up. Let's go, go, go, go.

1391
01:33:14,755 --> 01:33:15,589
What are you saying?
I just got here...

1392
01:33:15,673 --> 01:33:17,008
[Eun-sil] Go, go.

1393
01:33:17,883 --> 01:33:19,051
Seriously.

1394
01:33:19,135 --> 01:33:20,636
- Then get some rest.
- [Eun-sil] Seriously.

1395
01:33:20,720 --> 01:33:22,138
[Ha-min's aunt] What is this?

1396
01:33:22,221 --> 01:33:24,932
He only just woke up, so what are you...

1397
01:33:25,016 --> 01:33:26,058
[Eun-sil] Go. Hurry.

1398
01:33:26,767 --> 01:33:28,185
[door thuds]

1399
01:33:28,769 --> 01:33:30,021
[friend 1] Sigh.

1400
01:33:30,104 --> 01:33:31,188
Are you okay?

1401
01:33:31,731 --> 01:33:32,565
Yeah.

1402
01:33:32,648 --> 01:33:34,025
Hey, the doctor says it's a miracle.

1403
01:33:34,859 --> 01:33:36,193
He says you only need six rounds of chemo.

1404
01:33:38,070 --> 01:33:41,157
Hey, so your sister-in-law prepared
a gift for you.

1405
01:33:42,033 --> 01:33:43,701
What do you mean, sister-in-law?
Just because it's not your life...

1406
01:33:43,784 --> 01:33:44,702
Ahp.

1407
01:33:45,494 --> 01:33:46,329
Ahp?

1408
01:33:48,080 --> 01:33:50,875
Seeing you say "ahp, ahp" again
means you're well enough now.

1409
01:33:52,209 --> 01:33:53,252
[Ha-min] Ah...

1410
01:33:54,920 --> 01:33:56,797
- Goodness, damn it.
- [friend 2] Hey, now.

1411
01:33:57,715 --> 01:33:58,549
[friend 1 clears throat]

1412
01:33:58,632 --> 01:33:59,842
Thank you for surviving.

1413
01:33:59,925 --> 01:34:00,760
Yeah.

1414
01:34:04,013 --> 01:34:04,889
Here.

1415
01:34:07,391 --> 01:34:08,267
Look at this.

1416
01:34:11,937 --> 01:34:14,023
Hello, this is Park Mak-rye.

1417
01:34:14,106 --> 01:34:15,191
Hey, you damn punk.

1418
01:34:15,274 --> 01:34:18,152
Even if you roll around like dog poop,
isn't this world better than the afterlife?

1419
01:34:18,235 --> 01:34:20,363
Looking at your face,
you'll live a long life.

1420
01:34:20,446 --> 01:34:22,073
Listen to your mother.

1421
01:34:22,156 --> 01:34:23,115
Why are you making a fuss?

1422
01:34:23,199 --> 01:34:25,409
Is it because you don't listen
to your mom?

1423
01:34:25,493 --> 01:34:28,204
Think of Grandma's words as a bonus
and accept it.

1424
01:34:28,287 --> 01:34:29,622
Live well.

1425
01:34:29,705 --> 01:34:32,208
[Ha-min laughing and groaning]

1426
01:34:32,291 --> 01:34:33,542
[friend 1] Hey, are you okay?

1427
01:34:34,752 --> 01:34:35,878
[Ha-min] Ah, haha...

1428
01:34:35,961 --> 01:34:37,463
[birds chirping]

1429
01:34:42,009 --> 01:34:43,886
- Oh.
- Bean sprouts?

1430
01:34:43,969 --> 01:34:45,971
Yeah. Here.

1431
01:34:48,182 --> 01:34:50,142
- Green onion.
- [Ryeo-eun] How much green onion?

1432
01:34:50,768 --> 01:34:51,602
A lot.

1433
01:34:51,685 --> 01:34:52,978
How much is "a lot"?

1434
01:34:53,813 --> 01:34:54,647
Plenty.

1435
01:34:55,272 --> 01:34:57,274
Are we in Busan or Osaka?

1436
01:34:58,984 --> 01:35:00,444
Okay.

1437
01:35:05,157 --> 01:35:06,909
[Eun-sil] She's good with her hands.
Really good.

1438
01:35:06,992 --> 01:35:08,869
[Ha-min] Here it is.

1439
01:35:08,953 --> 01:35:09,912
[Ryeo-eun] Oh.

1440
01:35:09,995 --> 01:35:10,830
[Ha-min] Yes.

1441
01:35:12,039 --> 01:35:13,457
Ahp, wait.

1442
01:35:14,500 --> 01:35:16,710
- [Eun-sil] Oh, right.
- Oppa, close your eyes quickly.

1443
01:35:16,794 --> 01:35:17,670
Okay.

1444
01:35:19,338 --> 01:35:20,673
[Ha-min breathing nervously]

1445
01:35:20,756 --> 01:35:22,466
[calm music]

1446
01:35:25,010 --> 01:35:27,513
[Ryeo-eun] What is the last food
you'd want to eat from your mom?

1447
01:35:30,891 --> 01:35:32,017
Beef soup.

1448
01:35:32,101 --> 01:35:34,520
Then how about you make that
for your mom?

1449
01:35:35,479 --> 01:35:38,232
The home-cooked meals
your mom makes for you may only have one left,

1450
01:35:38,315 --> 01:35:41,026
but the home-cooked meals
you make for her can be infinite.

1451
01:35:44,071 --> 01:35:44,989
[Ha-min's father] But...

1452
01:35:45,614 --> 01:35:47,992
fate can change, you know?

1453
01:35:52,705 --> 01:35:54,999
Okay, try it.

1454
01:36:30,993 --> 01:36:33,037
[mysterious music]

1455
01:36:36,207 --> 01:36:37,124
It went up.

1456
01:36:39,293 --> 01:36:40,669
It went up.

1457
01:36:41,378 --> 01:36:42,796
- Really?
- [Eun-sil] Really?

1458
01:36:45,216 --> 01:36:46,967
Now, let's hurry and eat.

1459
01:36:47,051 --> 01:36:48,802
[Eun-sil laughing]

1460
01:36:51,222 --> 01:36:52,806
Oh my, mother-in-law.

1461
01:36:52,890 --> 01:36:54,892
- Why?
- [Ryeo-eun] Pardon?

1462
01:37:05,402 --> 01:37:06,904
Mom, give me some more broth.

1463
01:37:06,987 --> 01:37:08,489
It's good, right? Amazing, right?

1464
01:37:09,323 --> 01:37:10,407
[Eun-sil laughing]

1465
01:37:11,450 --> 01:37:12,952
Yeah, me too.

1466
01:37:16,789 --> 01:37:18,666
[softly] But it is a little bland.

1467
01:37:18,749 --> 01:37:19,917
But it's still good, right?

1468
01:37:20,501 --> 01:37:21,544
It is good.

1469
01:37:43,107 --> 01:37:44,608
Whew...

1470
01:37:49,947 --> 01:37:51,073
Ah...

1471
01:38:28,277 --> 01:38:30,279
[lyrical music]

1472
01:39:15,908 --> 01:39:16,909
[Daughter] Is it good?

1473
01:39:19,536 --> 01:39:20,412
It's good.

1474
01:39:21,288 --> 01:39:22,498
[Son] Eat like you're enjoying it, Mom.

1475
01:39:23,332 --> 01:39:24,833
[son laughing]

1476
01:39:43,394 --> 01:39:45,145
More than this soup my daughter made me,

1477
01:39:45,229 --> 01:39:47,147
I wish she'd show me her face more often.

1478
01:39:47,231 --> 01:39:48,941
Come home more often, my daughter.

1479
01:40:45,998 --> 01:40:46,832
Was yours good?

1480
01:40:46,915 --> 01:40:48,125
[Daughter] Should we post this
in the group chat?

1481
01:40:48,208 --> 01:40:49,668
Of course. Something like this
has to be posted.

1482
01:40:55,466 --> 01:40:57,593
[lyrical music continues]

1483
01:41:16,069 --> 01:41:19,573
[family]
♪ Congratulations, dear... ♪

1484
01:41:19,656 --> 01:41:22,576
[family] ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

1485
01:41:22,659 --> 01:41:23,535
[Mom] Oh~

1486
01:43:25,532 --> 01:43:28,243
Kids, thank you.
You worked hard preparing all this.

1487
01:43:28,327 --> 01:43:29,411
I enjoyed the meal.